window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-01-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3"]={"id":"CGL-01-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3","title":"CGL 01 OCT 2026 SHIFT 3","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000070081","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Find the WRONG number in the series.<br>11.2, 16.8, 42, 146, 661.5 [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"श्रेणी में गलत संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>11.2, 16.8, 42, 146, 661.5 [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"146"},"2":{"en":"16.8"},"3":{"en":"42"},"4":{"en":"11.2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The terms are multiplied by 1.5, then 2.5, then 3.5 and then 4.5: 11.2 × 1.5 = 16.8 ✔, 16.8 × 2.5 = 42 ✔<br>Next, 42 × 3.5 = 147, so the correct term is 147 and not 146 ✘<br>Checking the last step, 147 × 4.5 = 661.5 ✔, which fits the pattern exactly<br>Hence the wrong number in the series is 146<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 146.</b>","hi":"पद क्रमशः 1.5, फिर 2.5, फिर 3.5 तथा फिर 4.5 से गुणा होते हैं: 11.2 × 1.5 = 16.8 ✔, 16.8 × 2.5 = 42 ✔<br>इसके बाद 42 × 3.5 = 147 है, अतः सही पद 147 है, 146 नहीं ✘<br>अंतिम चरण जाँचने पर 147 × 4.5 = 661.5 ✔, जो पैटर्न से ठीक मेल खाता है<br>इसलिए श्रेणी में गलत संख्या 146 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 146 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000070082","section":"REASONING","topic":"Dice & Cube","question":{"en":"A cube is formed by folding the sheet. Which letter would be on the face opposite to 'M'?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/0197a5db-8dd9-797c-a03c-a481d57dabd3_EN.jpg?edu=639294370213578856\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"चादर को मोड़कर एक घन बनाया जाता है। 'M' के विपरीत फलक पर कौन-सा अक्षर होगा?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/0197a5db-8dd9-797c-a03c-a481d57dabd3_HI.jpg?edu=639294370329097521\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"E"},"2":{"en":"K"},"3":{"en":"U"},"4":{"en":"G"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In the net S, M and U lie in one straight line with one face between them, so S and U are opposite each other<br>E, K and G lie in another straight line with one face between them, so E and G are opposite each other<br>The two faces left are M and K, so they must be opposite each other<br>Hence K is on the face opposite to M<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): K.</b>","hi":"जाल में S, M तथा U एक सीधी रेखा में हैं और उनके बीच एक फलक है, अतः S और U परस्पर विपरीत हैं<br>E, K तथा G दूसरी सीधी रेखा में हैं और उनके बीच एक फलक है, अतः E और G परस्पर विपरीत हैं<br>शेष दो फलक M और K बचते हैं, अतः वे परस्पर विपरीत होंगे<br>इसलिए M के विपरीत फलक पर K है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): K है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/0197a5db-8dd9-797c-a03c-a481d57dabd3_EN.jpg?edu=639294370213578856","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/0197a5db-8dd9-797c-a03c-a481d57dabd3_HI.jpg?edu=639294370329097521"]}},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000070083","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Choose the roll number with even digits only. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"वह रोल नंबर चुनिए जिसमें केवल सम अंक हों। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"234x446"},"2":{"en":"135x357"},"3":{"en":"468x864"},"4":{"en":"579x975"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"An even digit is 0, 2, 4, 6 or 8, so every digit of the roll number must come from this set<br>In 234x446 the digits 3 is odd, in 135x357 the digits 1, 3, 5, 3, 5, 7 are all odd and in 579x975 the digits 5, 7, 9, 9, 7, 5 are all odd<br>Only in 468x864 the digits 4, 6, 8, 8, 6, 4 are all even ✔<br>Hence 468x864 is the roll number with even digits only<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 468x864.</b>","hi":"सम अंक 0, 2, 4, 6 या 8 होते हैं, अतः रोल नंबर का प्रत्येक अंक इसी समुच्चय से होना चाहिए<br>234x446 में अंक 3 विषम है, 135x357 में 1, 3, 5, 3, 5, 7 सभी विषम हैं तथा 579x975 में 5, 7, 9, 9, 7, 5 सभी विषम हैं<br>केवल 468x864 में अंक 4, 6, 8, 8, 6, 4 सभी सम हैं ✔<br>इसलिए 468x864 वह रोल नंबर है जिसमें केवल सम अंक हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 468x864 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000070084","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Find the odd one out.<br>Ganga, Yamuna, Godavari, Everest [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"विषम विकल्प ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>Ganga, Yamuna, Godavari, Everest [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ganga","hi":"गंगा"},"2":{"en":"Yamuna","hi":"यमुना"},"3":{"en":"Godavari","hi":"गोदावरी"},"4":{"en":"Everest","hi":"एवरेस्ट"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Ganga, Yamuna and Godavari are all rivers of India<br>Everest is a mountain peak and not a river, so it is different from the rest<br>Hence Everest is the odd one out<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Everest.</b>","hi":"गंगा, यमुना तथा गोदावरी सभी भारत की नदियाँ हैं<br>एवरेस्ट एक पर्वत शिखर है, नदी नहीं, अतः वह शेष से भिन्न है<br>इसलिए एवरेस्ट विषम है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): एवरेस्ट है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000070085","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"<b>Statements:</b><br>1. The Indian Museum in Kolkata, established in 1814, is one of the oldest and most important museums in India.<br>2. It is fully funded and managed by the Central Government, under the Ministry of Culture.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. The Indian Museum is a centrally administered cultural institution.<br>II. All museums in India were established before 1900. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कथन:<br>1. कोलकाता का भारतीय संग्रहालय, जो 1814 में स्थापित हुआ, भारत के सबसे पुराने और सबसे महत्वपूर्ण संग्रहालयों में से एक है।<br>2. यह पूरी तरह केंद्र सरकार द्वारा, संस्कृति मंत्रालय के अंतर्गत वित्तपोषित और प्रबंधित है।<br>निष्कर्ष:<br>I. भारतीय संग्रहालय एक केंद्रीय रूप से प्रशासित सांस्कृतिक संस्थान है।<br>II. भारत के सभी संग्रहालय 1900 से पहले स्थापित हुए थे। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Both conclusion I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The museum is funded and managed by the Central Government under the Ministry of Culture, which means it is centrally administered and cultural, so conclusion I follows ✔<br>The statements speak only about the Indian Museum and say nothing about all the museums of India, so conclusion II does not follow ✘<br>Hence only conclusion I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only conclusion I follows.</b>","hi":"संग्रहालय केंद्र सरकार द्वारा संस्कृति मंत्रालय के अंतर्गत वित्तपोषित तथा प्रबंधित है, जिसका अर्थ है कि वह केंद्रीय रूप से प्रशासित और सांस्कृतिक है, अतः निष्कर्ष I निकलता है ✔<br>कथन केवल भारतीय संग्रहालय के बारे में हैं और भारत के सभी संग्रहालयों के बारे में कुछ नहीं कहते, अतः निष्कर्ष II नहीं निकलता ✘<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000070086","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"<b>Instruction:</b> Identify the assumptions that must hold for the statement to be valid, then choose the correct option.<br><b>Statement:</b> Despite the challenges faced by renewable energy sources, they are the only long-term solution to our dependency on fossil fuels.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Renewable energy sources face certain challenges.<br>II. Fossil fuels are not a sustainable long-term solution.<br>III. Renewable energy sources can entirely replace fossil fuels. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निर्देश: वे अवधारणाएँ पहचानिए जो कथन के वैध होने के लिए आवश्यक हैं, फिर सही विकल्प चुनिए।<br>कथन: नवीकरणीय ऊर्जा स्रोतों के सामने मौजूद चुनौतियों के बावजूद, जीवाश्म ईंधनों पर हमारी निर्भरता का एकमात्र दीर्घकालिक समाधान वही हैं।<br>अवधारणाएँ:<br>I. नवीकरणीय ऊर्जा स्रोतों को कुछ चुनौतियों का सामना करना पड़ता है।<br>II. जीवाश्म ईंधन दीर्घकालिक टिकाऊ समाधान नहीं हैं।<br>III. नवीकरणीय ऊर्जा स्रोत जीवाश्म ईंधनों का पूरी तरह स्थान ले सकते हैं। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I and II are implicit","hi":"केवल I और II निहित हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only II and III are implicit","hi":"केवल II और III निहित हैं"},"3":{"en":"All are implicit","hi":"सभी निहित हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only I is implicit","hi":"केवल I निहित है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The statement begins by accepting that renewable sources face challenges, so assumption I must hold for the statement to be meaningful ✔<br>Calling renewable sources the only long-term solution presupposes that fossil fuels cannot be the long-term solution, so assumption II is implicit ✔<br>The statement speaks of a long-term solution and not of a complete replacement of fossil fuels today, so the word entirely makes assumption III too strong ✘<br>Hence only I and II are implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only I and II are implicit.</b>","hi":"कथन स्वयं कहता है कि नवीकरणीय स्रोतों को चुनौतियाँ हैं, अतः कथन के अर्थपूर्ण होने के लिए अवधारणा I आवश्यक है ✔<br>नवीकरणीय स्रोतों को एकमात्र दीर्घकालिक समाधान कहना यह मान लेता है कि जीवाश्म ईंधन दीर्घकालिक समाधान नहीं हैं, अतः अवधारणा II निहित है ✔<br>कथन दीर्घकालिक समाधान की बात करता है, आज पूर्ण प्रतिस्थापन की नहीं, अतः 'पूरी तरह' शब्द अवधारणा III को अत्यधिक बना देता है ✘<br>इसलिए केवल I और II निहित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल I और II निहित हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000070087","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Which of the following is/are identical to the address given:<br>Shruti Mehta 3/6, Lotus Avenue, Lucknow, 226007<br>1. Shruti Mehta 3/6, Lotus Avenue, Lucknow, 226007<br>2. Shruti Mehta 3/6, Lotus Avenue, Lucknow, 226007<br>3. Shruti Mehta 3/6, Lotus Avenue, Lucknow, 226008<br>4. Shruti Mehta 3/6, Lotus Avenue, New Lucknow, 226007 [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा/से दिए गए पते के समान है/हैं:<br>Shruti Mehta 3/6, Lotus Avenue, Lucknow, 226007<br>1. Shruti Mehta 3/6, Lotus Avenue, Lucknow, 226007<br>2. Shruti Mehta 3/6, Lotus Avenue, Lucknow, 226007<br>3. Shruti Mehta 3/6, Lotus Avenue, Lucknow, 226008<br>4. Shruti Mehta 3/6, Lotus Avenue, New Lucknow, 226007 [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2"},"2":{"en":"1 and 3","hi":"1 और 3"},"3":{"en":"2 and 4","hi":"2 और 4"},"4":{"en":"3 and 4","hi":"3 और 4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The given address has the house number 3/6, Lotus Avenue, the city Lucknow and the pin code 226007<br>Entries 1 and 2 repeat every part of the address exactly ✔<br>Entry 3 changes the pin code to 226008 and entry 4 changes the city to New Lucknow ✘<br>Hence 1 and 2 are identical to the given address<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1 and 2.</b>","hi":"दिए गए पते में मकान संख्या 3/6, Lotus Avenue, शहर Lucknow तथा पिन कोड 226007 है<br>प्रविष्टि 1 और 2 पते के प्रत्येक भाग को ठीक वैसा ही दोहराती हैं ✔<br>प्रविष्टि 3 में पिन कोड 226008 है तथा प्रविष्टि 4 में शहर New Lucknow है ✘<br>इसलिए 1 और 2 दिए गए पते के समान हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 और 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000070088","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Find the next number in the sequence.<br>2, 5, 10, 17, ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"क्रम में अगली संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>2, 5, 10, 17, ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"24"},"2":{"en":"26"},"3":{"en":"28"},"4":{"en":"30"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The differences are 3, 5 and 7, which are consecutive odd numbers<br>So the next difference is 9, and the next term is 17 + 9 = 26<br>Hence the next number is 26<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 26.</b>","hi":"अंतर 3, 5 तथा 7 हैं, जो क्रमागत विषम संख्याएँ हैं<br>अतः अगला अंतर 9 है और अगला पद 17 + 9 = 26 है<br>इसलिए अगली संख्या 26 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 26 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000070089","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Find the most suitable pair:<br>Ramayana &#8211; Ved Vyasa, Macbeth &#8211; Leo Tolstoy, Hamlet &#8211; Charles Dickens, War and Peace &#8211; William Shakespeare, Gitanjali &#8211; Rabindranath Tagore [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त युग्म ज्ञात कीजिए:<br>Ramayana &#8211; Ved Vyasa, Macbeth &#8211; Leo Tolstoy, Hamlet &#8211; Charles Dickens, War and Peace &#8211; William Shakespeare, Gitanjali &#8211; Rabindranath Tagore [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hamlet &#8211; Charles Dickens"},"2":{"en":"Macbeth &#8211; Leo Tolstoy"},"3":{"en":"War and Peace &#8211; William Shakespeare"},"4":{"en":"Gitanjali &#8211; Rabindranath Tagore"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The pair must put a work with its real author<br>Ramayana was written by Valmiki and not Ved Vyasa, Macbeth by Shakespeare and not Tolstoy, Hamlet by Shakespeare and not Dickens, and War and Peace by Tolstoy and not Shakespeare<br>Gitanjali was written by Rabindranath Tagore, so this pair is correct ✔<br>Hence Gitanjali &#8211; Rabindranath Tagore is the most suitable pair<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Gitanjali &#8211; Rabindranath Tagore.</b>","hi":"युग्म में कृति के साथ उसका वास्तविक रचनाकार होना चाहिए<br>रामायण वाल्मीकि ने लिखी, वेद व्यास ने नहीं; Macbeth शेक्सपियर की है, टॉल्स्टॉय की नहीं; Hamlet शेक्सपियर की है, डिकेंस की नहीं; और War and Peace टॉल्स्टॉय की है, शेक्सपियर की नहीं<br>Gitanjali रवींद्रनाथ टैगोर ने लिखी, अतः यह युग्म सही है ✔<br>इसलिए Gitanjali &#8211; Rabindranath Tagore सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त युग्म है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): Gitanjali &#8211; Rabindranath Tagore है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000070090","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Complete the series.<br>Z9, X8, V7, T6, ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"श्रेणी पूरी कीजिए।<br>Z9, X8, V7, T6, ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"R5"},"2":{"en":"S5"},"3":{"en":"Q5"},"4":{"en":"P5"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The letters move two places back each time: Z&#8594;X&#8594;V&#8594;T, so the next letter is R<br>The numbers decrease by one each time: 9, 8, 7, 6, so the next number is 5<br>Hence the next term is R5<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): R5.</b>","hi":"अक्षर प्रत्येक बार दो स्थान पीछे जाते हैं: Z&#8594;X&#8594;V&#8594;T, अतः अगला अक्षर R है<br>संख्याएँ प्रत्येक बार एक कम होती हैं: 9, 8, 7, 6, अतः अगली संख्या 5 है<br>इसलिए अगला पद R5 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): R5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000070091","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If \"SUN\" is coded as \"19 21 14\", how will \"MOON\" be coded? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि \"SUN\" का कूट \"19 21 14\" है, तो \"MOON\" का कूट क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12 14 14 13"},"2":{"en":"14 16 16 15"},"3":{"en":"13 15 15 14"},"4":{"en":"11 13 13 12"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Each letter is written as its alphabet position: S = 19, U = 21 and N = 14, which gives 19 21 14 ✔<br>So MOON is written as M = 13, O = 15, O = 15 and N = 14<br>Hence MOON is coded as 13 15 15 14<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 13 15 15 14.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर को उसके वर्णमाला स्थान के रूप में लिखा जाता है: S = 19, U = 21 तथा N = 14, जिससे 19 21 14 मिलता है ✔<br>अतः MOON को M = 13, O = 15, O = 15 तथा N = 14 लिखा जाएगा<br>इसलिए MOON का कूट 13 15 15 14 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 13 15 15 14 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000070092","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Find the INCORRECT number in the series.<br>5, 15, 45, 125, 405 [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"श्रेणी में गलत संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>5, 15, 45, 125, 405 [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15"},"2":{"en":"45"},"3":{"en":"125"},"4":{"en":"405"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Every term is three times the term before it: 5 × 3 = 15 ✔, 15 × 3 = 45 ✔<br>Next, 45 × 3 = 135, so the term 125 is wrong ✘, and 135 × 3 = 405 ✔ matches the last term<br>Hence the incorrect number in the series is 125<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 125.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद अपने पहले के पद का तीन गुना है: 5 × 3 = 15 ✔, 15 × 3 = 45 ✔<br>इसके बाद 45 × 3 = 135 है, अतः पद 125 गलत है ✘, और 135 × 3 = 405 ✔ अंतिम पद से मेल खाता है<br>इसलिए श्रेणी में गलत संख्या 125 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 125 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000070093","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"What is the total number of people surveyed?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/0197f907-91ba-7914-9055-68903ee28562_EN.jpg?edu=639294370214923593\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"सर्वेक्षण किए गए लोगों की कुल संख्या क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/0197f907-91ba-7914-9055-68903ee28562_HI.jpg?edu=639294370330139170\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"450"},"2":{"en":"550"},"3":{"en":"650"},"4":{"en":"750"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The diagram gives Hindi 450, English 300, both Hindi and English 200 and neither 100<br>The number who know at least one language is 450 + 300 − 200 = 550<br>Adding the 100 people who know neither language gives 550 + 100 = 650<br>Hence the total number of people surveyed is 650<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 650.</b>","hi":"आरेख में हिंदी 450, अंग्रेज़ी 300, दोनों 200 तथा कोई नहीं 100 दिया है<br>कम से कम एक भाषा जानने वालों की संख्या 450 + 300 − 200 = 550 है<br>कोई भाषा न जानने वाले 100 जोड़ने पर 550 + 100 = 650 मिलता है<br>इसलिए सर्वेक्षण किए गए लोगों की कुल संख्या 650 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 650 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/0197f907-91ba-7914-9055-68903ee28562_EN.jpg?edu=639294370214923593","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/0197f907-91ba-7914-9055-68903ee28562_HI.jpg?edu=639294370330139170"]}},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000070094","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"How many students study only Physics?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/0197f922-218b-7d7a-a398-83483d9f0441_EN.jpg?edu=639294370215132282\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कितने विद्यार्थी केवल भौतिकी पढ़ते हैं?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/0197f922-218b-7d7a-a398-83483d9f0441_HI.jpg?edu=639294370330300218\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25"},"2":{"en":"30"},"3":{"en":"20"},"4":{"en":"15"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The Physics circle has 60 in all, which includes the Physics and Chemistry overlap 20, the Physics and Math overlap 15 and the common part 5 of all three<br>The students who study only Physics are 60 − 20 − 15 + 5 = 30<br>Hence 30 students study only Physics<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 30.</b>","hi":"भौतिकी के वृत्त में कुल 60 हैं, जिसमें भौतिकी तथा रसायन का अतिव्यापी भाग 20, भौतिकी तथा गणित का 15 तथा तीनों का साझा भाग 5 शामिल है<br>केवल भौतिकी पढ़ने वाले विद्यार्थी 60 − 20 − 15 + 5 = 30 हैं<br>इसलिए 30 विद्यार्थी केवल भौतिकी पढ़ते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 30 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/0197f922-218b-7d7a-a398-83483d9f0441_EN.jpg?edu=639294370215132282","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/0197f922-218b-7d7a-a398-83483d9f0441_HI.jpg?edu=639294370330300218"]}},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000070095","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Identify the figure that does not belong to the group, based on shape.<br>&#9711; &#9711; &#9711; &#9632; [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आकार के आधार पर वह आकृति पहचानिए जो समूह में नहीं आती।<br>&#9711; &#9711; &#9711; &#9632; [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"&#9632;"},"2":{"en":"&#9711;"},"3":{"en":"&#9711;"},"4":{"en":"&#9711;"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Three of the four figures are hollow circles and one figure is a filled square<br>The filled square is different both in shape and in shading, so it does not belong to the group<br>Hence the filled square is the figure that does not belong to the group<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): &#9632;.</b>","hi":"चार आकृतियों में से तीन खोखले वृत्त हैं और एक भरा हुआ वर्ग है<br>भरा हुआ वर्ग आकार तथा छायांकन दोनों में भिन्न है, अतः वह समूह में नहीं आता<br>इसलिए भरा हुआ वर्ग वह आकृति है जो समूह में नहीं आती<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): &#9632; है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000070096","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A shop sells pens at &#8377;12 each and notebooks at &#8377;30 each. If a customer buys 3 pens and 2 notebooks, what's the total cost? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक दुकान पेन 12 रुपये प्रति पेन तथा नोटबुक 30 रुपये प्रति नोटबुक बेचती है। यदि कोई ग्राहक 3 पेन तथा 2 नोटबुक खरीदता है, तो कुल लागत क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"&#8377;96","hi":"96 रुपये"},"2":{"en":"&#8377;114","hi":"114 रुपये"},"3":{"en":"&#8377;102","hi":"102 रुपये"},"4":{"en":"&#8377;108","hi":"108 रुपये"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The cost of 3 pens is 3 × 12 = &#8377;36<br>The cost of 2 notebooks is 2 × 30 = &#8377;60<br>Adding both, the total cost is 36 + 60 = &#8377;96<br>Hence the total cost is &#8377;96<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): &#8377;96.</b>","hi":"3 पेन की लागत 3 × 12 = 36 रुपये है<br>2 नोटबुक की लागत 2 × 30 = 60 रुपये है<br>दोनों जोड़ने पर कुल लागत 36 + 60 = 96 रुपये है<br>इसलिए कुल लागत 96 रुपये है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 96 रुपये है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000070097","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, two groups of letters are related by a specific pattern. Identify the same pattern and apply it to the second group to find the missing letters.<br>ACD : BFJ :: FGH : ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में अक्षरों के दो समूह एक विशिष्ट पैटर्न से संबंधित हैं। वही पैटर्न पहचानिए और दूसरे समूह पर लागू करके लुप्त अक्षर ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>ACD : BFJ :: FGH : ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"GIN"},"2":{"en":"GJO"},"3":{"en":"GJN"},"4":{"en":"HIL"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In ACD : BFJ the letters move ahead by 1, 3 and 6 places: A(1) → B(2), C(3) → F(6) and D(4) → J(10)<br>Applying the same steps to FGH: F(6) → G(7), G(7) → J(10) and H(8) → N(14)<br>Hence the missing letters are GJN<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): GJN.</b>","hi":"ACD : BFJ में अक्षर 1, 3 तथा 6 स्थान आगे जाते हैं: A(1) → B(2), C(3) → F(6) तथा D(4) → J(10)<br>FGH पर वही चरण लगाने से F(6) → G(7), G(7) → J(10) तथा H(8) → N(14)<br>इसलिए लुप्त अक्षर GJN हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): GJN है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000070098","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"How many letters will remain at the same position in the word 'PROBLEM' when the letters are arranged in alphabetical order from left to right? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"शब्द 'PROBLEM' के अक्षरों को बाएँ से दाएँ वर्णमाला क्रम में व्यवस्थित करने पर कितने अक्षर अपने स्थान पर ही रहेंगे? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"PROBLEM has the letters P, R, O, B, L, E and M, whose alphabetical order is B, E, L, M, O, P and R<br>Comparing place by place, P→B, R→E, O→L, B→M, L→O, E→P and M→R, so no letter keeps its old place<br>Hence 0 letters remain at the same position<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 0.</b>","hi":"PROBLEM में अक्षर P, R, O, B, L, E तथा M हैं, जिनका वर्णमाला क्रम B, E, L, M, O, P तथा R है<br>स्थान-दर-स्थान तुलना करने पर P→B, R→E, O→L, B→M, L→O, E→P तथा M→R, अतः कोई अक्षर अपने पुराने स्थान पर नहीं रहता<br>इसलिए 0 अक्षर अपने स्थान पर रहते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 0 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000070099","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"Identify the alternative set of numbers that correctly codes the word. The code uses [Row, Column] format.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">F</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">R</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">J</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">E</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">M</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">D</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">S</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">B</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">O</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">T</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">L</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">E</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">R</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">C</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">A</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">N</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">D</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">E</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">P</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">J</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">U</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">M</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">B</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">L</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Y</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">O</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">W</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">O</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">N</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">D</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">E</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">R</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">S</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">G</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">A</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">R</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">D</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">E</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">N</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">X</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">P</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">L</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">A</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">N</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">E</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">T</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Q</td></tr></table><br>What is the correct code for \"MANIFEST\"? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"संख्याओं का वह विकल्प समुच्चय पहचानिए जो शब्द को सही ढंग से कूटबद्ध करता है। कूट [पंक्ति, स्तंभ] प्रारूप में है।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">F</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">R</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">J</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">E</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">M</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">D</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">S</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">B</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">O</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">T</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">L</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">E</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">R</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">C</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">A</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">N</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">D</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">E</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">P</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">J</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">U</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">M</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">B</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">L</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Y</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">O</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">W</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">O</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">N</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">D</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">E</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">R</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">S</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">G</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">A</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">R</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">D</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">E</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">N</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">X</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">P</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">L</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">A</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">N</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">E</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">T</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Q</td></tr></table><br>\"MANIFEST\" के लिए सही कूट क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(4,3)(3,2)(7,4)(3,5)(3,1)(2,5)(5,7)(4,3)"},"2":{"en":"(4,3)(3,2)(7,4)(3,5)(1,4)(2,6)(5,6)(2,4)"},"3":{"en":"(4,3)(3,2)(7,4)(3,5)(1,1)(2,6)(5,7)(2,3)"},"4":{"en":"(4,3)(3,2)(7,4)(3,5)(4,1)(3,1)(5,6)(2,7)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Reading the grid by rows and columns: M is at row 4, column 3; A is at row 3, column 2; N is at row 7, column 4; I is at row 3, column 5<br>Next, F is at row 1, column 1; E is at row 2, column 6; S is at row 5, column 7 and T is at row 2, column 3<br>Joining the coordinates gives (4,3)(3,2)(7,4)(3,5)(1,1)(2,6)(5,7)(2,3)<br>Hence the third set of numbers codes MANIFEST correctly<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): (4,3)(3,2)(7,4)(3,5)(1,1)(2,6)(5,7)(2,3).</b>","hi":"ग्रिड को पंक्तियों तथा स्तंभों से पढ़ने पर: M पंक्ति 4, स्तंभ 3 पर; A पंक्ति 3, स्तंभ 2 पर; N पंक्ति 7, स्तंभ 4 पर; I पंक्ति 3, स्तंभ 5 पर है<br>इसके बाद F पंक्ति 1, स्तंभ 1 पर; E पंक्ति 2, स्तंभ 6 पर; S पंक्ति 5, स्तंभ 7 पर तथा T पंक्ति 2, स्तंभ 3 पर है<br>निर्देशांक जोड़ने पर (4,3)(3,2)(7,4)(3,5)(1,1)(2,6)(5,7)(2,3) मिलता है<br>इसलिए तीसरा संख्या-समुच्चय MANIFEST को सही ढंग से कूटबद्ध करता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): (4,3)(3,2)(7,4)(3,5)(1,1)(2,6)(5,7)(2,3) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000070100","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You're working on a team project, and a colleague asks you to cover for them by saying they were in a meeting with you yesterday afternoon, when in fact they left early without informing the manager. What should you do? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आप एक टीम परियोजना पर काम कर रहे हैं और एक सहकर्मी आपसे कहता है कि आप उसके लिए यह कहकर बचाव करें कि वह कल दोपहर आपके साथ बैठक में था, जबकि वास्तव में वह प्रबंधक को बताए बिना जल्दी चला गया था। आपको क्या करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Agree to cover for them since they're a friend and would do the same for you.","hi":"उनका बचाव करने के लिए हामी भरना, क्योंकि वे मित्र हैं और आपके लिए भी वही करते।"},"2":{"en":"Politely decline, and tell them you're not comfortable being dishonest if asked.","hi":"विनम्रता से मना करना और यह बताना कि पूछे जाने पर झूठ बोलना आपको असहज लगेगा।"},"3":{"en":"Immediately report your colleague to the manager.","hi":"सहकर्मी की शिकायत तुरंत प्रबंधक से करना।"},"4":{"en":"Ignore the request and avoid the colleague going forward.","hi":"अनुरोध को अनसुना करना और आगे उस सहकर्मी से बचते रहना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Covering with a false statement makes you part of the dishonesty and puts your own credibility at risk<br>Declining politely and saying clearly that you will not lie if asked keeps your honesty intact and still treats the colleague with respect<br>Agreeing, reporting at once or quietly avoiding the person either creates a lie, escalates the issue or damages the relationship without any need<br>Hence politely declining and being clear about not being dishonest is the right response<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Politely decline, and tell them you're not comfortable being dishonest if asked..</b>","hi":"झूठे कथन से बचाव करना आपको भी उस बेईमानी का हिस्सा बना देता है और आपकी विश्वसनीयता जोखिम में डालता है<br>विनम्रता से मना करना और स्पष्ट कहना कि पूछे जाने पर आप झूठ नहीं बोलेंगे, आपकी ईमानदारी बनाए रखता है और सहकर्मी का सम्मान भी<br>हामी भरना, तुरंत शिकायत करना या चुपचाप उससे बचते रहना — ये क्रमशः झूठ बनाते हैं, मामला बढ़ा देते हैं या बिना आवश्यकता संबंध बिगाड़ देते हैं<br>अतः विनम्रता से मना करना और ईमानदार न रहने की बात स्पष्ट करना सही प्रतिक्रिया है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): विनम्रता से मना करना और यह बताना कि पूछे जाने पर झूठ बोलना आपको असहज लगेगा। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000070101","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br>Question Figures:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/019ed377-3604-7c9f-a4a7-5c42761dc284_EN.jpg?edu=639294370216989513\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]<br>Answer Figures: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक विशिष्ट संबंध है। तीसरी तथा चौथी आकृति के बीच वही संबंध स्थापित करने के लिए दी गई उत्तर आकृतियों में से उपयुक्त आकृति चुनकर प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर रखिए।<br>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/019ed377-3604-7c9f-a4a7-5c42761dc284_HI.jpg?edu=639294370331718157\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]<br>उत्तर आकृतियाँ: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In the first pair the circle is divided into four parts by a cross and the small marks placed in the outer parts move inwards, and the whole figure is rotated a quarter turn<br>So the change is that the inner marks take one step round the circle while the divisions stay the same<br>Answer figure 3 shows the circle with the same divisions and the marks shifted in exactly this way<br>Hence answer figure 3 replaces the question mark<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 3.</b>","hi":"पहले युग्म में वृत्त को एक क्रॉस से चार भागों में बाँटा गया है और बाहरी भागों में रखे छोटे चिह्न भीतर की ओर आ जाते हैं, तथा पूरी आकृति एक चौथाई घूम जाती है<br>अतः परिवर्तन यह है कि भीतरी चिह्न वृत्त के चारों ओर एक चरण आगे बढ़ते हैं जबकि विभाजन वही रहते हैं<br>उत्तर आकृति 3 में वही विभाजन हैं और चिह्न ठीक इसी प्रकार खिसके हैं<br>इसलिए उत्तर आकृति 3 प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न के स्थान पर आएगी<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/019ed377-3604-7c9f-a4a7-5c42761dc284_EN.jpg?edu=639294370216989513","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/019ed377-3604-7c9f-a4a7-5c42761dc284_HI.jpg?edu=639294370331718157"]}},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000070102","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br>Question Figures:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/019ed382-09f0-73a0-8412-7d421de26392_EN.jpg?edu=639294370217310515\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]<br>Answer Figures: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक विशिष्ट संबंध है। तीसरी तथा चौथी आकृति के बीच वही संबंध स्थापित करने के लिए दी गई उत्तर आकृतियों में से उपयुक्त आकृति चुनकर प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर रखिए।<br>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/019ed382-09f0-73a0-8412-7d421de26392_HI.jpg?edu=639294370331966685\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]<br>उत्तर आकृतियाँ: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In the first pair a single large dark circle becomes two dark circles placed side by side, so the number of dark parts doubles and the parts become half in size<br>In the third figure a single dark rectangle must in the same way become two dark rectangles of half the size placed side by side<br>Answer figure 1 shows two equal dark rectangles in one row, exactly the required change<br>Hence answer figure 1 replaces the question mark<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"पहले युग्म में एक बड़ा काला वृत्त दो काले वृत्तों में बदल जाता है जो साथ-साथ रखे हैं, अतः काले भागों की संख्या दोगुनी और आकार आधा हो जाता है<br>तीसरी आकृति में एक काला आयत उसी प्रकार आधे आकार के दो काले आयतों में बदलना चाहिए जो साथ-साथ हों<br>उत्तर आकृति 1 में एक पंक्ति में दो बराबर काले आयत हैं, जो ठीक आवश्यक परिवर्तन है<br>इसलिए उत्तर आकृति 1 प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न के स्थान पर आएगी<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/019ed382-09f0-73a0-8412-7d421de26392_EN.jpg?edu=639294370217310515","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/019ed382-09f0-73a0-8412-7d421de26392_HI.jpg?edu=639294370331966685"]}},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000070103","section":"REASONING","topic":"Embedded Figures","question":{"en":"In the following question, select the alternative figure which is embedded in the given fig. (X).<br>Figure(X):<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/019ed49e-aabb-7dab-84f2-2484187a6b6c_EN.jpg?edu=639294370217636736\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]<br>Alternative figures: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में वह वैकल्पिक आकृति चुनिए जो दी गई आकृति (X) में अंतर्निहित है।<br>आकृति (X):<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/019ed49e-aabb-7dab-84f2-2484187a6b6c_HI.jpg?edu=639294370332228375\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]<br>वैकल्पिक आकृतियाँ: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"3"},"3":{"en":"4"},"4":{"en":"1"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Figure (X) is a circle with a fan of straight lines meeting near the top and a set of slanting lines below, which together make many small angular shapes<br>The embedded figure must appear among these lines with exactly the same shape and the same slant<br>Only figure 3, the M-shaped angular figure with a peak in the middle, is traced exactly by the lines of figure (X), while the other alternatives need curves or proportions that the figure does not contain<br>Hence figure 3 is embedded in figure (X)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 3.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) एक वृत्त है जिसमें ऊपर के पास मिलती सीधी रेखाओं का पंखा तथा नीचे तिर्यक रेखाएँ हैं, जो मिलकर अनेक छोटी कोणीय आकृतियाँ बनाती हैं<br>अंतर्निहित आकृति इन रेखाओं में ठीक उसी आकार और उसी ढाल के साथ मिलनी चाहिए<br>केवल आकृति 3, जो बीच में शिखर वाली M जैसी कोणीय आकृति है, आकृति (X) की रेखाओं से ठीक बनती है, जबकि अन्य विकल्पों के लिए वक्र या अनुपात चाहिए जो आकृति में नहीं हैं<br>इसलिए आकृति 3, आकृति (X) में अंतर्निहित है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/019ed49e-aabb-7dab-84f2-2484187a6b6c_EN.jpg?edu=639294370217636736","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/019ed49e-aabb-7dab-84f2-2484187a6b6c_HI.jpg?edu=639294370332228375"]}},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000070104","section":"REASONING","topic":"Counting Figures","question":{"en":"How many triangles are there in the given figure?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/019ed612-f6ff-7fbc-80e8-dfc29ee249ee_EN.jpg?edu=639294370217721523\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई आकृति में कितने त्रिभुज हैं?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/019ed612-f6ff-7fbc-80e8-dfc29ee249ee_HI.jpg?edu=639294370332492624\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"27"},"2":{"en":"25"},"3":{"en":"19"},"4":{"en":"15"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The figure is a large triangle with its inner triangle joining the mid points and the three corner triangles again divided by lines to the centre<br>Counting the small triangles gives 9 in the inner part, the triangles made of two small parts add 9, those made of three small parts add 6 and the two large triangles add 3<br>Adding them, 9 + 9 + 6 + 3 = 27<br>Hence there are 27 triangles in the figure<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 27.</b>","hi":"आकृति एक बड़ा त्रिभुज है जिसका भीतरी त्रिभुज मध्य बिंदुओं को जोड़ता है और तीनों कोने के त्रिभुज केंद्र तक की रेखाओं से फिर बँटे हैं<br>छोटे त्रिभुज गिनने पर भीतरी भाग में 9 मिलते हैं, दो छोटे भागों से बने त्रिभुज 9, तीन छोटे भागों से बने 6 तथा बड़े त्रिभुज 3<br>जोड़ने पर 9 + 9 + 6 + 3 = 27<br>इसलिए आकृति में 27 त्रिभुज हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 27 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/019ed612-f6ff-7fbc-80e8-dfc29ee249ee_EN.jpg?edu=639294370217721523","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/019ed612-f6ff-7fbc-80e8-dfc29ee249ee_HI.jpg?edu=639294370332492624"]}},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000070105","section":"REASONING","topic":"Embedded Figures","question":{"en":"Carefully observe Figure (X) and identify the option figure in which Figure (X) is embedded exactly as shown.<br>Figure X:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/019f032b-4330-78a2-a68b-d9f4e74ef9ff_EN.jpg?edu=639294370217767870\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]<br>Answer Figures: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आकृति (X) को ध्यान से देखिए और वह विकल्प आकृति पहचानिए जिसमें आकृति (X) ठीक वैसी ही अंतर्निहित है।<br>आकृति X:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/019f032b-4330-78a2-a68b-d9f4e74ef9ff_HI.jpg?edu=639294370332772705\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]<br>उत्तर आकृतियाँ: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Figure (X) is the letter W drawn with three straight strokes: a long line coming down from the top left to the lowest point, a line rising to a middle peak and a line falling again, all strokes of almost equal length<br>The embedded figure must have the same three strokes with the same angles and the same length<br>Option figure 3 shows the square with this tall W inside it, traced exactly by its lines<br>The other options contain a cross inside a square, vertical parallel lines or diagonals meeting at the centre, which cannot give this W shape<br>Hence figure (X) is embedded in option figure 3<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 3.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) अक्षर W है जो तीन सीधे स्पर्शों से बना है: बाएँ ऊपर से नीचे के निम्नतम बिंदु तक आती लंबी रेखा, फिर मध्य शिखर तक उठती रेखा तथा फिर गिरती रेखा, और सभी स्पर्श लगभग बराबर लंबाई के हैं<br>अंतर्निहित आकृति में वही तीन स्पर्श, वही कोण तथा वही लंबाई होनी चाहिए<br>विकल्प आकृति 3 में वर्ग के भीतर यही लंबा W है, जो उसकी रेखाओं से ठीक बनता है<br>अन्य विकल्पों में वर्ग के भीतर क्रॉस, ऊर्ध्व समांतर रेखाएँ या केंद्र पर मिलते विकर्ण हैं, जो यह W आकृति नहीं दे सकते<br>अतः आकृति (X) विकल्प आकृति 3 में अंतर्निहित है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/019f032b-4330-78a2-a68b-d9f4e74ef9ff_EN.jpg?edu=639294370217767870","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/019f032b-4330-78a2-a68b-d9f4e74ef9ff_HI.jpg?edu=639294370332772705"]}}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000070106","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Stone Age","question":{"en":"In which period did humans first start making and using pottery? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"मनुष्यों ने सबसे पहले किस काल में मिट्टी के बर्तन बनाना और उपयोग करना शुरू किया? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Neolithic Age","hi":"नवपाषाण काल"},"2":{"en":"Mesolithic Age","hi":"मध्यपाषाण काल"},"3":{"en":"Palaeolithic Age","hi":"पुरापाषाण काल"},"4":{"en":"Chalcolithic Age","hi":"ताम्रपाषाण काल"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Neolithic Age</b><br><b>Pottery</b> first appeared with settled farming life in the <b><u>Neolithic Age</u></b>, when people needed vessels to store grain and cook food. Early pots were hand-made, and later the potter's wheel came into use.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Neolithic features: <b>agriculture, domestication of animals, polished stone tools</b> and permanent settlements.<br>• <b>Mehrgarh</b> (Balochistan) is the earliest Neolithic site in the subcontinent; <b>Burzahom</b> (Kashmir) had pit dwellings.<br>• <b>Chalcolithic Age</b> – first use of copper along with stone.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – नवपाषाण काल</b><br><b>मिट्टी के बर्तन</b> सबसे पहले <b><u>नवपाषाण काल</u></b> में स्थायी कृषि जीवन के साथ बने, जब लोगों को अनाज रखने और भोजन पकाने के लिए पात्रों की आवश्यकता हुई। प्रारंभिक बर्तन हाथ से बने, बाद में कुम्हार के चाक का उपयोग शुरू हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• नवपाषाण विशेषताएँ: <b>कृषि, पशुपालन, पॉलिशदार पत्थर के औज़ार</b> और स्थायी बस्तियाँ।<br>• <b>मेहरगढ़</b> (बलूचिस्तान) उपमहाद्वीप का सबसे प्राचीन नवपाषाण स्थल है; <b>बुर्ज़होम</b> (कश्मीर) में गर्त-आवास मिले।<br>• <b>ताम्रपाषाण काल</b> – पत्थर के साथ पहली बार ताँबे का उपयोग।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000070107","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Post-Maurya Dynasties","question":{"en":"To which of these groups did the ambassador Heliodorus, who built the pillar at Vidisha, belong? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"विदिशा में स्तंभ बनवाने वाला राजदूत हेलियोडोरस इनमें से किस समूह से संबंधित था? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Parthian Kingdom","hi":"पार्थियन राज्य"},"2":{"en":"The Kushan Kingdom","hi":"कुषाण राज्य"},"3":{"en":"The Indo-Greek Kingdom","hi":"हिंद-यवन (इंडो-ग्रीक) राज्य"},"4":{"en":"The Indo-Scythian Kingdom","hi":"हिंद-शक (इंडो-सीथियन) राज्य"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – The Indo-Greek Kingdom</b><br><b>Heliodorus</b> was the ambassador of the <b><u>Indo-Greek</u></b> king <b>Antialcidas</b> of Taxila to the court of the Shunga ruler <b>Bhagabhadra</b>. He erected the <b>Garuda Pillar (Heliodorus Pillar)</b> at Besnagar near Vidisha in honour of Vasudeva.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The pillar (c. 113 BCE) is one of the earliest evidences of <b>Bhagavata (Vaishnava)</b> worship; Heliodorus calls himself a <b>Bhagavata</b>.<br>• The most famous Indo-Greek ruler was <b>Menander (Milinda)</b>, mentioned in <b>Milindapanho</b>.<br>• Indo-Greeks were the first to issue <b>gold coins</b> in India.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – हिंद-यवन (इंडो-ग्रीक) राज्य</b><br><b>हेलियोडोरस</b> तक्षशिला के <b><u>हिंद-यवन (Indo-Greek)</u></b> राजा <b>एंटियालसिडस</b> का राजदूत था, जो शुंग शासक <b>भागभद्र</b> के दरबार में आया। उसने वासुदेव के सम्मान में विदिशा के निकट बेसनगर में <b>गरुड़ स्तंभ (हेलियोडोरस स्तंभ)</b> बनवाया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह स्तंभ (लगभग 113 ई.पू.) <b>भागवत (वैष्णव)</b> उपासना के सबसे प्राचीन प्रमाणों में से है; हेलियोडोरस स्वयं को <b>भागवत</b> कहता है।<br>• सबसे प्रसिद्ध हिंद-यवन शासक <b>मिनांडर (मिलिंद)</b> था, जिसका उल्लेख <b>मिलिंदपन्हो</b> में है।<br>• हिंद-यवनों ने भारत में सबसे पहले <b>सोने के सिक्के</b> जारी किए।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000070108","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: The Mughal Empire","question":{"en":"What does the term “jama” refer to in the Mughal revenue system? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"मुग़ल राजस्व व्यवस्था में “जमा” शब्द किसे दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Actual revenue collected during the year.","hi":"वर्ष के दौरान वास्तव में एकत्र राजस्व।"},"2":{"en":"Estimated revenue assessed from an area.","hi":"किसी क्षेत्र से आकलित अनुमानित राजस्व।"},"3":{"en":"Tax-free land grant to religious institutions.","hi":"धार्मिक संस्थाओं को कर-मुक्त भूमि अनुदान।"},"4":{"en":"Revenue assigned to jagirdars.","hi":"जागीरदारों को सौंपा गया राजस्व।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Estimated revenue assessed from an area.</b><br>In the Mughal system, <b>jama</b> was the <b><u>amount of revenue assessed (estimated)</u></b> from an area, while <b>hasil</b> was the amount actually collected.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Akbar's revenue system <b>Zabti / Dahsala (1580)</b> was developed by <b>Raja Todar Mal</b>.<br>• <b>Madad-i-maash / Suyurghal</b> – tax-free land grants to scholars and religious persons.<br>• <b>Jagir</b> – revenue assignment given to mansabdars in place of salary.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – किसी क्षेत्र से आकलित अनुमानित राजस्व।</b><br>मुग़ल व्यवस्था में <b>जमा</b> किसी क्षेत्र से <b><u>आकलित (अनुमानित) राजस्व</u></b> की राशि थी, जबकि <b>हासिल</b> वास्तव में एकत्र की गई राशि थी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अकबर की राजस्व व्यवस्था <b>ज़ब्ती / दहसाला (1580)</b> <b>राजा टोडरमल</b> ने विकसित की।<br>• <b>मदद-ए-माश / सुयूरग़ाल</b> – विद्वानों और धार्मिक व्यक्तियों को कर-मुक्त भूमि अनुदान।<br>• <b>जागीर</b> – वेतन के स्थान पर मनसबदारों को दिया गया राजस्व क्षेत्र।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000070109","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"According to Article 60 of the Indian Constitution, who administers the oath of office to the President of India? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 60 के अनुसार भारत के राष्ट्रपति को पद की शपथ कौन दिलाता है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Prime Minister","hi":"प्रधानमंत्री"},"2":{"en":"Vice President","hi":"उपराष्ट्रपति"},"3":{"en":"Chief Justice of India","hi":"भारत के मुख्य न्यायाधीश"},"4":{"en":"Speaker of the Lok Sabha","hi":"लोकसभा अध्यक्ष"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Chief Justice of India</b><br>Under <b>Article 60</b>, the oath to the President is administered by the <b><u>Chief Justice of India</u></b>, and in his absence by the <b>senior-most judge</b> of the Supreme Court.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The President swears to <b>\"preserve, protect and defend the Constitution and the law\"</b>.<br>• The <b>Vice-President</b> is administered oath by the <b>President</b> (Article 69).<br>• The President administers oath to the <b>Prime Minister, Union Ministers and CJI</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – भारत के मुख्य न्यायाधीश</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 60</b> के तहत राष्ट्रपति को शपथ <b><u>भारत के मुख्य न्यायाधीश</u></b> दिलाते हैं और उनकी अनुपस्थिति में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के <b>वरिष्ठतम न्यायाधीश</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• राष्ट्रपति <b>\"संविधान और विधि का परिरक्षण, संरक्षण और प्रतिरक्षण\"</b> करने की शपथ लेते हैं।<br>• <b>उपराष्ट्रपति</b> को शपथ <b>राष्ट्रपति</b> दिलाते हैं (अनुच्छेद 69)।<br>• राष्ट्रपति <b>प्रधानमंत्री, केंद्रीय मंत्रियों और मुख्य न्यायाधीश</b> को शपथ दिलाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000070110","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"Which article of the Constitution of India states that a person must have completed the age of 35 years to be eligible for election as President? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत के संविधान का कौन-सा अनुच्छेद कहता है कि राष्ट्रपति के रूप में निर्वाचन हेतु पात्र होने के लिए व्यक्ति को 35 वर्ष की आयु पूरी करनी होगी? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 52","hi":"अनुच्छेद 52"},"2":{"en":"Article 66","hi":"अनुच्छेद 66"},"3":{"en":"Article 58","hi":"अनुच्छेद 58"},"4":{"en":"Article 84","hi":"अनुच्छेद 84"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Article 58</b><br><b><u>Article 58</u></b> lays down the qualifications for election as President: a <b>citizen of India</b>, who has <b>completed 35 years</b>, and is qualified for election as a member of the Lok Sabha.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 52</b> – There shall be a President of India.<br>• <b>Article 66</b> – election of the Vice-President (also 35 years).<br>• <b>Article 84</b> – qualification for Parliament: 30 years for Rajya Sabha, 25 years for Lok Sabha.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अनुच्छेद 58</b><br><b><u>अनुच्छेद 58</u></b> राष्ट्रपति के निर्वाचन की योग्यताएँ बताता है: <b>भारत का नागरिक</b> हो, <b>35 वर्ष पूरे</b> कर चुका हो और लोकसभा सदस्य के रूप में निर्वाचन के योग्य हो।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 52</b> – भारत का एक राष्ट्रपति होगा।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 66</b> – उपराष्ट्रपति का निर्वाचन (आयु भी 35 वर्ष)।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 84</b> – संसद सदस्यता की योग्यता: राज्यसभा के लिए 30 वर्ष, लोकसभा के लिए 25 वर्ष।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000070111","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"Under Article 111 of the Indian Constitution, what does the President's \"Suspensive Veto\" power allow him to do in relation to a Bill passed by Parliament? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 111 के तहत राष्ट्रपति की \"निलंबनकारी वीटो\" शक्ति उन्हें संसद द्वारा पारित विधेयक के संबंध में क्या करने की अनुमति देती है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Withhold the Bill indefinitely","hi":"विधेयक को अनिश्चित काल तक रोकना"},"2":{"en":"Return the Bill for reconsideration","hi":"विधेयक को पुनर्विचार के लिए लौटाना"},"3":{"en":"Reject the Bill permanently","hi":"विधेयक को स्थायी रूप से अस्वीकार करना"},"4":{"en":"Refer the Bill to the Supreme Court","hi":"विधेयक को सर्वोच्च न्यायालय को भेजना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Return the Bill for reconsideration</b><br>Under <b>suspensive veto</b>, the President can <b><u>return a non-money Bill to Parliament for reconsideration</u></b>. If Parliament passes it again, with or without amendments, the President must give assent.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The President has three vetoes: <b>Absolute, Suspensive and Pocket veto</b>.<br>• <b>Pocket veto</b> was used by President <b>Zail Singh</b> on the Indian Post Office (Amendment) Bill, 1986.<br>• Suspensive veto <b>cannot</b> be used for Money Bills or Constitutional Amendment Bills.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – विधेयक को पुनर्विचार के लिए लौटाना</b><br><b>निलंबनकारी वीटो (Suspensive veto)</b> के तहत राष्ट्रपति <b><u>धन विधेयक के अतिरिक्त किसी विधेयक को पुनर्विचार के लिए संसद को लौटा</u></b> सकते हैं। संसद द्वारा संशोधन सहित या रहित दोबारा पारित होने पर राष्ट्रपति को स्वीकृति देनी होती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• राष्ट्रपति के पास तीन वीटो हैं: <b>आत्यंतिक, निलंबनकारी और जेबी वीटो (Absolute, Suspensive, Pocket veto)</b>।<br>• <b>जेबी वीटो</b> का प्रयोग राष्ट्रपति <b>ज्ञानी ज़ैल सिंह</b> ने भारतीय डाकघर (संशोधन) विधेयक, 1986 पर किया।<br>• निलंबनकारी वीटो धन विधेयकों या संविधान संशोधन विधेयकों पर <b>लागू नहीं</b> होता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000070112","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Making of Constitution","question":{"en":"In which month was Pitt's India Act of 1784 passed? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पिट्स इंडिया एक्ट, 1784 किस महीने में पारित हुआ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"June","hi":"जून"},"2":{"en":"August","hi":"अगस्त"},"3":{"en":"September","hi":"सितंबर"},"4":{"en":"March","hi":"मार्च"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – August</b><br><b>Pitt's India Act</b>, named after British PM <b>William Pitt the Younger</b>, received royal assent on <b>13 <u>August</u> 1784</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It set up the <b>Board of Control</b> to supervise the Company's political affairs – a <b>system of double government</b>.<br>• Commercial affairs remained with the <b>Court of Directors</b>.<br>• It was enacted to remove the defects of the <b>Regulating Act, 1773</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अगस्त</b><br>ब्रिटिश प्रधानमंत्री <b>विलियम पिट द यंगर</b> के नाम पर <b>पिट्स इंडिया एक्ट</b> को <b>13 <u>अगस्त</u> 1784</b> को शाही स्वीकृति मिली।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसने कंपनी के राजनीतिक मामलों की निगरानी के लिए <b>नियंत्रण बोर्ड (Board of Control)</b> बनाया – <b>द्वैध शासन प्रणाली</b>।<br>• वाणिज्यिक मामले <b>निदेशक मंडल (Court of Directors)</b> के पास रहे।<br>• इसे <b>रेगुलेटिंग एक्ट, 1773</b> की कमियाँ दूर करने के लिए लाया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000070113","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Wind, Ocean Current, and Cyclone","question":{"en":"<b>Fill in the blank:</b><br>The _______ effect describes the deflection of moving objects (like winds and ocean currents) to the right in the Northern Hemisphere due to Earth's rotation. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>रिक्त स्थान भरिए:</b><br>_______ प्रभाव पृथ्वी के घूर्णन के कारण उत्तरी गोलार्ध में गतिमान वस्तुओं (जैसे पवनें और महासागरीय धाराएँ) के दाईं ओर विक्षेपण का वर्णन करता है। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Doppler","hi":"डॉप्लर"},"2":{"en":"Coriolis","hi":"कोरिऑलिस"},"3":{"en":"Greenhouse","hi":"ग्रीनहाउस"},"4":{"en":"Tyndall","hi":"टिंडल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Coriolis</b><br>The <b><u>Coriolis effect</u></b>, caused by the Earth's rotation, deflects winds and currents to the <b>right in the Northern Hemisphere</b> and to the <b>left in the Southern Hemisphere</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Named after French scientist <b>Gaspard-Gustave de Coriolis</b> (1835); the law of wind deflection is <b>Ferrel's Law</b>.<br>• Coriolis force is <b>maximum at the poles</b> and <b>zero at the Equator</b>, so cyclones do not form near the Equator.<br>• <b>Doppler effect</b> – change in frequency due to relative motion; <b>Tyndall effect</b> – scattering of light by colloidal particles.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – कोरिऑलिस</b><br>पृथ्वी के घूर्णन से उत्पन्न <b><u>कोरिऑलिस प्रभाव</u></b> पवनों और धाराओं को <b>उत्तरी गोलार्ध में दाईं ओर</b> और <b>दक्षिणी गोलार्ध में बाईं ओर</b> मोड़ता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• फ्रांसीसी वैज्ञानिक <b>गैस्पार्ड-गुस्ताव डी कोरिऑलिस</b> (1835) के नाम पर; पवन विक्षेपण का नियम <b>फेरल का नियम</b> है।<br>• कोरिऑलिस बल <b>ध्रुवों पर अधिकतम</b> और <b>भूमध्य रेखा पर शून्य</b> होता है, इसलिए भूमध्य रेखा के पास चक्रवात नहीं बनते।<br>• <b>डॉप्लर प्रभाव</b> – सापेक्ष गति से आवृत्ति में परिवर्तन; <b>टिंडल प्रभाव</b> – कोलॉइडी कणों द्वारा प्रकाश का प्रकीर्णन।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000070114","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"In which of the following states is the Anthurium Festival celebrated? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से किस राज्य में एंथुरियम उत्सव मनाया जाता है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Kerala","hi":"केरल"},"2":{"en":"Mizoram","hi":"मिज़ोरम"},"3":{"en":"Sikkim","hi":"सिक्किम"},"4":{"en":"West Bengal","hi":"पश्चिम बंगाल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Mizoram</b><br>The <b>Anthurium Festival</b> is held in <b><u>Mizoram</u></b> (mainly at <b>Reiek</b> village) to promote tourism and showcase the anthurium flower, culture and cuisine of the state.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It is organised by Mizoram's Department of Tourism, usually in <b>September</b>.<br>• Other Mizoram festivals: <b>Chapchar Kut, Mim Kut, Pawl Kut</b>.<br>• <b>Hornbill Festival</b> – Nagaland; <b>Losoong</b> – Sikkim.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मिज़ोरम</b><br><b>एंथुरियम उत्सव</b> <b><u>मिज़ोरम</u></b> (मुख्यतः <b>रेइक</b> गाँव) में पर्यटन को बढ़ावा देने तथा एंथुरियम फूल, राज्य की संस्कृति और व्यंजनों को प्रदर्शित करने के लिए मनाया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसे मिज़ोरम का पर्यटन विभाग सामान्यतः <b>सितंबर</b> में आयोजित करता है।<br>• मिज़ोरम के अन्य त्योहार: <b>चापचार कुट, मिम कुट, पॉल कुट</b>।<br>• <b>हॉर्नबिल उत्सव</b> – नागालैंड; <b>लोसूंग</b> – सिक्किम।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000070115","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which principle makes an athlete responsible for any substance found in their sample? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कौन-सा सिद्धांत खिलाड़ी को उसके नमूने में पाए गए किसी भी पदार्थ के लिए उत्तरदायी बनाता है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Negligence","hi":"लापरवाही"},"2":{"en":"Strict Liability","hi":"कठोर दायित्व"},"3":{"en":"Intentionality","hi":"आशयपूर्णता"},"4":{"en":"Consent","hi":"सहमति"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Strict Liability</b><br>Under the <b>World Anti-Doping Code</b>, the principle of <b><u>strict liability</u></b> makes each athlete responsible for any prohibited substance found in his or her sample, whether or not it was used intentionally.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>WADA</b> was established in <b>1999</b>; HQ <b>Montreal, Canada</b>.<br>• India's <b>NADA</b> functions under the <b>National Anti-Doping Act, 2022</b>.<br>• WADA publishes the <b>Prohibited List</b> every year.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – कठोर दायित्व</b><br><b>विश्व डोपिंग रोधी संहिता</b> के तहत <b><u>कठोर दायित्व (Strict liability)</u></b> का सिद्धांत प्रत्येक खिलाड़ी को उसके नमूने में पाए गए किसी भी प्रतिबंधित पदार्थ के लिए उत्तरदायी बनाता है, चाहे उसका उपयोग जानबूझकर हुआ हो या नहीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>WADA</b> की स्थापना <b>1999</b> में हुई; मुख्यालय <b>मॉन्ट्रियल, कनाडा</b>।<br>• भारत का <b>NADA</b> <b>राष्ट्रीय डोपिंग रोधी अधिनियम, 2022</b> के तहत कार्य करता है।<br>• WADA हर वर्ष <b>प्रतिबंधित सूची (Prohibited List)</b> जारी करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000070116","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"Which of the following pairs of traditional folk dance and its associated state is <b>correctly</b> matched? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पारंपरिक लोक नृत्य और उससे संबद्ध राज्य का निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा युग्म <b>सही</b> सुमेलित है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gendi - Chhattisgarh","hi":"गेंडी - छत्तीसगढ़"},"2":{"en":"Cheraw - Kerala","hi":"चेराव - केरल"},"3":{"en":"Hojagiri - Sikkim","hi":"होजागिरी - सिक्किम"},"4":{"en":"Baredi – Nagaland","hi":"बरेदी – नागालैंड"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Gendi - Chhattisgarh</b><br><b><u>Gendi</u></b> is a folk dance of the <b>Gond (Muria) tribe of Chhattisgarh</b>, performed by young men balancing on tall bamboo stilts. So <b>Gendi – Chhattisgarh</b> is correctly matched.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Cheraw</b> (bamboo dance) – <b>Mizoram</b>.<br>• <b>Hojagiri</b> – <b>Tripura</b> (Reang community), performed balancing on earthen pitchers.<br>• <b>Baredi</b> – <b>Madhya Pradesh</b> (Bundelkhand), performed around Diwali.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – गेंडी - छत्तीसगढ़</b><br><b><u>गेंडी</u></b> <b>छत्तीसगढ़ की गोंड (मुरिया) जनजाति</b> का लोक नृत्य है, जिसमें युवक ऊँची बाँस की बल्लियों पर संतुलन बनाकर नाचते हैं। अतः <b>गेंडी – छत्तीसगढ़</b> सही सुमेलित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>चेराव</b> (बाँस नृत्य) – <b>मिज़ोरम</b>।<br>• <b>होजागिरी</b> – <b>त्रिपुरा</b> (रियांग समुदाय), मिट्टी के घड़ों पर संतुलन बनाकर किया जाता है।<br>• <b>बरेदी</b> – <b>मध्य प्रदेश</b> (बुंदेलखंड), दीपावली के आसपास किया जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000070117","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Which of the following terms refers to the primary form of compositions in the Carnatic music tradition? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा शब्द कर्नाटक संगीत परंपरा में रचनाओं के प्रमुख रूप को दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bandish","hi":"बंदिश"},"2":{"en":"Ghazal","hi":"ग़ज़ल"},"3":{"en":"Kriti","hi":"कृति"},"4":{"en":"Thumri","hi":"ठुमरी"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Kriti</b><br><b><u>Kriti</u></b> is the most important form of composition in <b>Carnatic music</b>. It has three parts – <b>Pallavi, Anupallavi and Charanam</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Carnatic Trinity</b>: <b>Tyagaraja, Muthuswami Dikshitar, Syama Sastri</b>.<br>• <b>Purandara Dasa</b> is called the \"Father of Carnatic Music\".<br>• <b>Bandish, Thumri</b> belong to Hindustani music; <b>Ghazal</b> is a poetic-musical form in Urdu/Persian.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – कृति</b><br><b><u>कृति</u></b> <b>कर्नाटक संगीत</b> में रचना का सबसे महत्वपूर्ण रूप है। इसके तीन भाग हैं – <b>पल्लवी, अनुपल्लवी और चरणम्</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>कर्नाटक त्रिमूर्ति (Trinity)</b>: <b>त्यागराज, मुत्तुस्वामी दीक्षितर, श्यामा शास्त्री</b>।<br>• <b>पुरंदर दास</b> को \"कर्नाटक संगीत का पितामह\" कहा जाता है।<br>• <b>बंदिश, ठुमरी</b> हिंदुस्तानी संगीत के रूप हैं; <b>ग़ज़ल</b> उर्दू/फ़ारसी का काव्य-संगीत रूप है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000070118","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Banking","question":{"en":"What is the main objective of RBI’s (Reserve Bank of India) Unified Lending Interface (ULI) initiative in India? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक (RBI) की एकीकृत ऋण इंटरफ़ेस (ULI) पहल का मुख्य उद्देश्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To replace UPI for digital payments","hi":"डिजिटल भुगतान के लिए UPI का स्थान लेना"},"2":{"en":"To enable inclusive and frictionless access to credit","hi":"ऋण तक समावेशी और सहज पहुँच संभव बनाना"},"3":{"en":"To regulate global cryptocurrency transactions","hi":"वैश्विक क्रिप्टोकरेंसी लेनदेन का विनियमन करना"},"4":{"en":"To manage central bank recruitment","hi":"केंद्रीय बैंक भर्ती का प्रबंधन करना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – To enable inclusive and frictionless access to credit</b><br>The <b>Unified Lending Interface (ULI)</b> is a digital platform that brings together borrower data (land records, income, etc.) through APIs to provide <b><u>frictionless, inclusive credit</u></b>, especially to farmers and MSMEs.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• ULI was announced by RBI Governor <b>Shaktikanta Das</b> in <b>August 2024</b>; developed by the <b>Reserve Bank Innovation Hub (RBIH)</b>.<br>• It is compared to <b>UPI</b> – \"ULI will do for lending what UPI did for payments\".<br>• Together <b>JAM-UPI-ULI</b> is called India's \"new trinity\" of digital public infrastructure.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ऋण तक समावेशी और सहज पहुँच संभव बनाना</b><br><b>एकीकृत ऋण इंटरफ़ेस (ULI)</b> एक डिजिटल प्लेटफ़ॉर्म है जो API के माध्यम से उधारकर्ता के आँकड़े (भूमि रिकॉर्ड, आय आदि) एक साथ लाकर विशेषकर किसानों और MSMEs को <b><u>सहज, समावेशी ऋण</u></b> उपलब्ध कराता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ULI की घोषणा RBI गवर्नर <b>शक्तिकांत दास</b> ने <b>अगस्त 2024</b> में की; इसे <b>रिज़र्व बैंक इनोवेशन हब (RBIH)</b> ने विकसित किया।<br>• इसकी तुलना <b>UPI</b> से की जाती है – \"ULI ऋण के लिए वही करेगा जो UPI ने भुगतान के लिए किया\"।<br>• <b>JAM-UPI-ULI</b> को डिजिटल सार्वजनिक अवसंरचना की \"नई त्रिमूर्ति\" कहा गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000070119","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Awards and Honours (Current)","question":{"en":"Which of the following author-language pairs (Poetry category) for the Sahitya Akademi Award 2025 is <b>correctly</b> matched? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025 (कविता श्रेणी) के लिए निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा लेखक-भाषा युग्म <b>सही</b> सुमेलित है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Sadhu Bhadreshdas – Urdu","hi":"साधु भद्रेशदास – उर्दू"},"2":{"en":"Pritpal Singh Betab – Sanskrit","hi":"प्रीतपाल सिंह बेताब – संस्कृत"},"3":{"en":"Nandini Sidha Reddy – Telugu","hi":"नंदिनी सिद्धा रेड्डी – तेलुगु"},"4":{"en":"Khajur Singh Thakur – Gujarati","hi":"खजूर सिंह ठाकुर – गुजराती"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Nandini Sidha Reddy – Telugu</b><br>Telangana poet <b><u>Nandini Sidha Reddy</u></b> was chosen for the <b>Sahitya Akademi Award 2025</b> in <b>Telugu</b> for his poetry; the awards for 24 languages were announced in <b>March 2026</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The award carries a <b>casket with an engraved copper plaque, a shawl and ₹1 lakh</b>.<br>• Sahitya Akademi was established on <b>12 March 1954</b>; HQ at <b>Rabindra Bhavan, New Delhi</b>.<br>• The Akademi gives awards in <b>24 languages</b> (22 Eighth Schedule languages plus English and Rajasthani).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – नंदिनी सिद्धा रेड्डी – तेलुगु</b><br>तेलंगाना के कवि <b><u>नंदिनी सिद्धा रेड्डी</u></b> को उनकी कविता के लिए <b>तेलुगु</b> भाषा में <b>साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025</b> हेतु चुना गया; 24 भाषाओं के पुरस्कारों की घोषणा <b>मार्च 2026</b> में हुई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पुरस्कार में <b>उत्कीर्ण ताम्रपत्र, शॉल और ₹1 लाख</b> दिए जाते हैं।<br>• साहित्य अकादमी की स्थापना <b>12 मार्च 1954</b> को हुई; मुख्यालय <b>रवींद्र भवन, नई दिल्ली</b>।<br>• अकादमी <b>24 भाषाओं</b> (आठवीं अनुसूची की 22 भाषाएँ तथा अंग्रेज़ी और राजस्थानी) में पुरस्कार देती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000070120","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which of the following <b>correctly</b> matches the width measurements of the pommel horse in gymnastics? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"जिम्नास्टिक्स में पॉमेल हॉर्स की चौड़ाई के मापों का निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा <b>सही</b> मिलान है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Top – 30 cm, Bottom – 35 cm","hi":"ऊपर – 30 cm, नीचे – 35 cm"},"2":{"en":"Top – 35 cm, Bottom – 30 cm","hi":"ऊपर – 35 cm, नीचे – 30 cm"},"3":{"en":"Top – 40 cm, Bottom – 35 cm","hi":"ऊपर – 40 cm, नीचे – 35 cm"},"4":{"en":"Top – 25 cm, Bottom – 30 cm","hi":"ऊपर – 25 cm, नीचे – 30 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Top – 35 cm, Bottom – 30 cm</b><br>As per FIG apparatus norms, the body of the pommel horse is <b><u>35 cm wide at the top and 30 cm at the bottom</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Length of the pommel horse is about <b>160 cm</b> and height about <b>115 cm</b>; pommels are <b>12 cm</b> high.<br>• Pommel horse is a <b>men's</b> artistic gymnastics event.<br>• Gymnastics is governed by <b>FIG</b> (Fédération Internationale de Gymnastique), HQ <b>Lausanne</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ऊपर – 35 cm, नीचे – 30 cm</b><br>FIG उपकरण मानकों के अनुसार पॉमेल हॉर्स का शरीर <b><u>ऊपर 35 cm और नीचे 30 cm चौड़ा</u></b> होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पॉमेल हॉर्स की लंबाई लगभग <b>160 cm</b> और ऊँचाई लगभग <b>115 cm</b> होती है; पॉमेल <b>12 cm</b> ऊँचे होते हैं।<br>• पॉमेल हॉर्स <b>पुरुषों</b> की कलात्मक जिम्नास्टिक्स स्पर्धा है।<br>• जिम्नास्टिक्स का शासी निकाय <b>FIG</b> है, मुख्यालय <b>लुसाने</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000070121","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: International Organisations","question":{"en":"The inclusion of Myanmar transformed BIST-EC (Bangladesh, India, Sri Lanka, Thailand Economic Cooperation) into: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"म्यांमार के शामिल होने से BIST-EC (बांग्लादेश, भारत, श्रीलंका, थाईलैंड आर्थिक सहयोग) किसमें परिवर्तित हो गया? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"BBIN (Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Nepal)","hi":"BBIN (बांग्लादेश, भूटान, भारत, नेपाल)"},"2":{"en":"BIMST-EC (Bangladesh, India, Myanmar, Sri Lanka, Thailand Economic Cooperation)","hi":"BIMST-EC (बांग्लादेश, भारत, म्यांमार, श्रीलंका, थाईलैंड आर्थिक सहयोग)"},"3":{"en":"ASEAN-EC (Association of Southeast Asian Nations Economic Cooperation)","hi":"ASEAN-EC (दक्षिण-पूर्व एशियाई राष्ट्र संघ आर्थिक सहयोग)"},"4":{"en":"BIMSTEC Plus (Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation Plus)","hi":"BIMSTEC प्लस (बहु-क्षेत्रीय तकनीकी और आर्थिक सहयोग हेतु बंगाल की खाड़ी पहल प्लस)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – BIMST-EC (Bangladesh, India, Myanmar, Sri Lanka, Thailand Economic Cooperation)</b><br>BIST-EC was formed on <b>6 June 1997</b> by the Bangkok Declaration. When <b>Myanmar</b> joined in <b>December 1997</b>, it became <b><u>BIMST-EC</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Nepal and Bhutan</b> joined in <b>2004</b>, and it was renamed <b>BIMSTEC</b> – Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation.<br>• Secretariat: <b>Dhaka, Bangladesh</b>; BIMSTEC has <b>7 members</b>.<br>• The BIMSTEC Charter came into force in <b>2024</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – BIMST-EC (बांग्लादेश, भारत, म्यांमार, श्रीलंका, थाईलैंड आर्थिक सहयोग)</b><br>BIST-EC का गठन <b>6 जून 1997</b> को बैंकॉक घोषणा द्वारा हुआ। <b>दिसंबर 1997</b> में <b>म्यांमार</b> के शामिल होने पर यह <b><u>BIMST-EC</u></b> बन गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>नेपाल और भूटान</b> <b>2004</b> में शामिल हुए और इसका नाम <b>BIMSTEC</b> – बहु-क्षेत्रीय तकनीकी और आर्थिक सहयोग हेतु बंगाल की खाड़ी पहल – रखा गया।<br>• सचिवालय: <b>ढाका, बांग्लादेश</b>; BIMSTEC के <b>7 सदस्य</b> हैं।<br>• BIMSTEC चार्टर <b>2024</b> में लागू हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000070122","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"Which of the following best defines a “document” under the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023 के तहत “दस्तावेज़” की सबसे उपयुक्त परिभाषा निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only written paper records signed by parties","hi":"केवल पक्षकारों द्वारा हस्ताक्षरित लिखित कागज़ी अभिलेख"},"2":{"en":"Only electronic records generated by computers","hi":"केवल कंप्यूटर द्वारा उत्पन्न इलेक्ट्रॉनिक अभिलेख"},"3":{"en":"Any matter recorded by letters, figures, marks, or electronic or digital means intended for recording matter","hi":"अक्षरों, अंकों, चिह्नों या इलेक्ट्रॉनिक अथवा डिजिटल साधनों द्वारा अभिलिखित कोई भी विषय, जो विषय को अभिलिखित करने के आशय से हो"},"4":{"en":"Only officially certified records","hi":"केवल आधिकारिक रूप से प्रमाणित अभिलेख"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Any matter recorded by letters, figures, marks, or electronic or digital means intended for recording matter</b><br><b>Section 2(1)(d) of the BSA, 2023</b> defines a document as <b><u>any matter expressed or described on any substance by letters, figures or marks, or by electronic or digital means</u></b>, intended to be used for recording that matter. It includes electronic and digital records.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Examples include emails, server logs, documents on computers, laptops or smartphones, messages, websites and voice mail.<br>• BSA replaced the <b>Indian Evidence Act, 1872</b> from <b>1 July 2024</b>.<br>• Electronic records are now treated as <b>primary evidence</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अक्षरों, अंकों, चिह्नों या इलेक्ट्रॉनिक अथवा डिजिटल साधनों द्वारा अभिलिखित कोई भी विषय, जो विषय को अभिलिखित करने के आशय से हो</b><br><b>BSA, 2023 की धारा 2(1)(d)</b> दस्तावेज़ को <b><u>किसी पदार्थ पर अक्षरों, अंकों या चिह्नों अथवा इलेक्ट्रॉनिक या डिजिटल साधनों द्वारा व्यक्त या वर्णित कोई भी विषय</u></b> बताती है, जिसका आशय उस विषय को अभिलिखित करना हो। इसमें इलेक्ट्रॉनिक और डिजिटल अभिलेख शामिल हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उदाहरणों में ईमेल, सर्वर लॉग, कंप्यूटर/लैपटॉप/स्मार्टफोन में दस्तावेज़, संदेश, वेबसाइट और वॉइस मेल शामिल हैं।<br>• BSA ने <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से <b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 1872</b> का स्थान लिया।<br>• इलेक्ट्रॉनिक अभिलेख अब <b>प्राथमिक साक्ष्य</b> माने जाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000070123","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who was appointed as Executive Director of the Reserve Bank of India with effect from March 3, 2026? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"3 मार्च 2026 से भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक के कार्यकारी निदेशक के रूप में किसे नियुक्त किया गया? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ajay Seth","hi":"अजय सेठ"},"2":{"en":"Sanjay Kumar Hansda","hi":"संजय कुमार हांसदा"},"3":{"en":"Rajeshwar Rao","hi":"राजेश्वर राव"},"4":{"en":"T. Rabi Sankar","hi":"टी. रबी शंकर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Sanjay Kumar Hansda</b><br>The RBI appointed <b><u>Sanjay Kumar Hansda</u></b> as <b>Executive Director</b> with effect from <b>3 March 2026</b>. He earlier served as an advisor at the <b>IMF</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• RBI was established on <b>1 April 1935</b> under the <b>RBI Act, 1934</b>; nationalised in <b>1949</b>.<br>• Current RBI Governor: <b>Sanjay Malhotra</b> (26<sup>th</sup> Governor, since December 2024).<br>• <b>T. Rabi Sankar</b> and <b>M. Rajeshwar Rao</b> have served as RBI Deputy Governors.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – संजय कुमार हांसदा</b><br>RBI ने <b><u>संजय कुमार हांसदा</u></b> को <b>3 मार्च 2026</b> से <b>कार्यकारी निदेशक</b> नियुक्त किया। वे पहले <b>IMF</b> में सलाहकार रह चुके हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• RBI की स्थापना <b>RBI अधिनियम, 1934</b> के तहत <b>1 अप्रैल 1935</b> को हुई; <b>1949</b> में राष्ट्रीयकरण।<br>• वर्तमान RBI गवर्नर: <b>संजय मल्होत्रा</b> (26वें गवर्नर, दिसंबर 2024 से)।<br>• <b>टी. रबी शंकर</b> और <b>एम. राजेश्वर राव</b> RBI के डिप्टी गवर्नर रह चुके हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000070124","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Human Geography","question":{"en":"Which of the following <b>correctly</b> identifies speech area overlap between Dravidian and Indo-Aryan groups? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा द्रविड़ और भारतीय-आर्य समूहों के बीच भाषा-क्षेत्र के अतिव्यापन की <b>सही</b> पहचान करता है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bihar appears in both Dravidian and Indo-Aryan lists","hi":"बिहार द्रविड़ और भारतीय-आर्य दोनों सूचियों में आता है"},"2":{"en":"Kerala appears in both Dravidian and Sino-Tibetan lists","hi":"केरल द्रविड़ और चीनी-तिब्बती दोनों सूचियों में आता है"},"3":{"en":"Assam appears in both Austric and Indo-Aryan lists","hi":"असम ऑस्ट्रिक और भारतीय-आर्य दोनों सूचियों में आता है"},"4":{"en":"Tamil Nadu appears in both Austric and Dravidian lists","hi":"तमिलनाडु ऑस्ट्रिक और द्रविड़ दोनों सूचियों में आता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Bihar appears in both Dravidian and Indo-Aryan lists</b><br>In the NCERT classification of Indian languages, <b><u>Bihar</u></b> is listed under the <b>North Dravidian</b> sub-group (Kurukh/Oraon, Malto) and also under <b>Indo-Aryan</b> (Bhojpuri, Maithili, Magahi). So Bihar is the area of overlap between the two groups.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Four language families in India: <b>Austric, Dravidian, Sino-Tibetan, Indo-European (Aryan)</b>.<br>• Indo-Aryan languages are spoken by about <b>73%</b> of Indians; Dravidian by about <b>20%</b>.<br>• The Dravidian family is divided into South, Central and North Dravidian; <b>Kerala and Tamil Nadu</b> fall under South Dravidian.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – बिहार द्रविड़ और भारतीय-आर्य दोनों सूचियों में आता है</b><br>NCERT के भारतीय भाषाओं के वर्गीकरण में <b><u>बिहार</u></b> को <b>उत्तरी द्रविड़</b> उप-समूह (कुडुख/उरांव, माल्टो) तथा <b>भारतीय-आर्य</b> (भोजपुरी, मैथिली, मगही) दोनों में रखा गया है। अतः दोनों समूहों का अतिव्यापन क्षेत्र बिहार है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत में चार भाषा परिवार: <b>ऑस्ट्रिक, द्रविड़, चीनी-तिब्बती, भारोपीय (आर्य)</b>।<br>• लगभग <b>73%</b> भारतीय भारतीय-आर्य भाषाएँ और लगभग <b>20%</b> द्रविड़ भाषाएँ बोलते हैं।<br>• द्रविड़ परिवार दक्षिणी, मध्य और उत्तरी द्रविड़ में बँटा है; <b>केरल और तमिलनाडु</b> दक्षिणी द्रविड़ में आते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000070125","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"<b>Fill in the blank:</b><br>Privatisation of public sector enterprises by selling off part of the equity of Public Sector Enterprise (PSE) to the public is known as_____. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>रिक्त स्थान भरिए:</b><br>सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र के उद्यम (PSE) की इक्विटी का एक भाग जनता को बेचकर सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र के उद्यमों के निजीकरण को _____ कहा जाता है। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"nationalisation","hi":"राष्ट्रीयकरण"},"2":{"en":"globalisation","hi":"वैश्वीकरण"},"3":{"en":"disinvestment","hi":"विनिवेश"},"4":{"en":"investment","hi":"निवेश"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – disinvestment</b><br>Selling a part of the government's equity in public sector enterprises to the public is called <b><u>disinvestment</u></b> (NCERT, Indian Economic Development).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Disinvestment is handled by <b>DIPAM</b> (Department of Investment and Public Asset Management) under the Ministry of Finance.<br>• PSUs were given <b>Maharatna, Navratna and Miniratna</b> status to improve efficiency.<br>• <b>Nationalisation</b> is the opposite – bringing private enterprises under government ownership (e.g., banks in 1969).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – विनिवेश</b><br>सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र के उद्यमों में सरकार की इक्विटी का एक भाग जनता को बेचना <b><u>विनिवेश (Disinvestment)</u></b> कहलाता है (NCERT, भारतीय आर्थिक विकास)।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• विनिवेश वित्त मंत्रालय के <b>DIPAM</b> (निवेश और सार्वजनिक परिसंपत्ति प्रबंधन विभाग) द्वारा किया जाता है।<br>• दक्षता बढ़ाने के लिए PSU को <b>महारत्न, नवरत्न और मिनीरत्न</b> का दर्जा दिया गया।<br>• <b>राष्ट्रीयकरण</b> इसका उल्टा है – निजी उद्यमों को सरकारी स्वामित्व में लाना (जैसे 1969 में बैंक)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000070126","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"Which of the following pollutants has only an annual National Ambient Air Quality Standard and is therefore not included in India’s routine Air Quality Index (AQI) calculation? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से किस प्रदूषक का केवल वार्षिक राष्ट्रीय परिवेशी वायु गुणवत्ता मानक है और इसलिए वह भारत के नियमित वायु गुणवत्ता सूचकांक (AQI) की गणना में शामिल नहीं है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ammonia\\((NH_3)\\)","hi":"अमोनिया\\((NH_3)\\)"},"2":{"en":"Ozone\\((O_3)\\)","hi":"ओज़ोन\\((O_3)\\)"},"3":{"en":"Carbon monoxide (CO)","hi":"कार्बन मोनोऑक्साइड (CO)"},"4":{"en":"Benzene \\((C_6H_6)\\)","hi":"बेंज़ीन \\((C_6H_6)\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Benzene \\((C_6H_6)\\)</b><br>The Air Quality Index is computed only for pollutants that have a <b>short-term (1-hour, 8-hour or 24-hour) standard</b> under the National Ambient Air Quality Standards. <b>Benzene</b> has only an <b>annual standard</b> of 5 µg/m³, so it is not used in the routine AQI calculation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The AQI is calculated from <b>eight pollutants</b> — PM10, PM2.5, nitrogen dioxide, sulphur dioxide, carbon monoxide, ozone, ammonia and lead.<br>• <b>Arsenic, nickel and benzo(a)pyrene</b> are the other NAAQS pollutants with only annual standards, so they too stay out of the AQI.<br>• The AQI converts each concentration into a sub-index from <b>0 to 500</b>, and the <b>worst sub-index</b> becomes the AQI of that station.<br>• NAAQS were notified by the <b>Central Pollution Control Board in 2009</b>, and the AQI was launched on <b>6 April 2015</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – बेंज़ीन \\((C_6H_6)\\)</b><br>वायु गुणवत्ता सूचकांक केवल उन्हीं प्रदूषकों हेतु निकाला जाता है जिनके राष्ट्रीय परिवेशी वायु गुणवत्ता मानक में <b>अल्पकालिक (1 घंटा, 8 घंटा या 24 घंटा) मानक</b> हैं। <b>बेंज़ीन</b> का केवल <b>वार्षिक मानक</b> 5 µg/m³ है, अतः वह नियमित AQI गणना में प्रयुक्त नहीं होता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• AQI <b>आठ प्रदूषकों</b> से निकाला जाता है — PM10, PM2.5, नाइट्रोजन डाइऑक्साइड, सल्फर डाइऑक्साइड, कार्बन मोनोऑक्साइड, ओज़ोन, अमोनिया तथा सीसा।<br>• <b>आर्सेनिक, निकेल तथा बेंज़ो(ए)पायरीन</b> NAAQS के अन्य ऐसे प्रदूषक हैं जिनके केवल वार्षिक मानक हैं, अतः वे भी AQI से बाहर हैं।<br>• AQI प्रत्येक सांद्रता को <b>0 से 500</b> तक के उप-सूचकांक में बदलता है और <b>सर्वाधिक प्रतिकूल उप-सूचकांक</b> उस केंद्र का AQI माना जाता है।<br>• NAAQS <b>2009</b> में केंद्रीय प्रदूषण नियंत्रण बोर्ड द्वारा अधिसूचित हुए तथा AQI <b>6 अप्रैल 2015</b> को आरंभ हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000070127","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"How much did the payload performance of the Small Satellite Launch Vehicle increase due to the first carbon-epoxy solid motor case used in its Solid Stage-3 motor during ISRO's 2025 Technology Demonstration tests? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"ISRO के 2025 प्रौद्योगिकी प्रदर्शन परीक्षणों के दौरान लघु उपग्रह प्रक्षेपण यान के ठोस चरण-3 मोटर में पहली बार कार्बन-एपॉक्सी ठोस मोटर केस के उपयोग से इसकी पेलोड क्षमता कितनी बढ़ी? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"40 kg"},"2":{"en":"60 kg"},"3":{"en":"90 kg"},"4":{"en":"120 kg"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 90 kg</b><br>ISRO's ground test of the improved <b>SSLV third stage (SS3)</b> with a <b>carbon-epoxy composite motor case</b> (December 2025) showed that the lighter case raises SSLV's payload capability by about <b><u>90 kg</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The test was conducted at <b>Satish Dhawan Space Centre, Sriharikota</b>.<br>• SSLV is a <b>three-stage, all-solid</b> launch vehicle with a liquid Velocity Trimming Module; it can place about <b>500 kg</b> in Low Earth Orbit.<br>• First successful SSLV flight: <b>SSLV-D2 (February 2023)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 90 kg</b><br>ISRO के <b>कार्बन-एपॉक्सी मिश्रित मोटर केस</b> वाले उन्नत <b>SSLV तृतीय चरण (SS3)</b> के ग्राउंड टेस्ट (दिसंबर 2025) से पता चला कि हल्के केस से SSLV की पेलोड क्षमता लगभग <b><u>90 kg</u></b> बढ़ती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• परीक्षण <b>सतीश धवन अंतरिक्ष केंद्र, श्रीहरिकोटा</b> में किया गया।<br>• SSLV <b>तीन चरणों वाला, पूर्णतः ठोस</b> प्रक्षेपण यान है, जिसमें द्रव वेलोसिटी ट्रिमिंग मॉड्यूल है; यह निम्न भू-कक्षा में लगभग <b>500 kg</b> स्थापित कर सकता है।<br>• SSLV की पहली सफल उड़ान: <b>SSLV-D2 (फरवरी 2023)</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000070128","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"What was a major architectural purpose of intricate jali work in Indo-Islamic buildings? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"हिंद-इस्लामी इमारतों में जटिल जाली कार्य का एक प्रमुख स्थापत्य उद्देश्य क्या था? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To increase structural weight and stability","hi":"संरचनात्मक भार और स्थिरता बढ़ाना"},"2":{"en":"To display abundant construction materials and wealth","hi":"प्रचुर निर्माण सामग्री और समृद्धि का प्रदर्शन करना"},"3":{"en":"To filter light while providing ventilation and privacy","hi":"वायु-संचार और गोपनीयता प्रदान करते हुए प्रकाश को छानना"},"4":{"en":"To determine building height and proportion","hi":"इमारत की ऊँचाई और अनुपात निर्धारित करना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – To filter light while providing ventilation and privacy</b><br><b>Jalis</b> (perforated stone screens) <b><u>filtered sunlight, allowed air to flow and gave privacy</u></b>, especially in zenanas, while also adding beauty with geometric and floral patterns.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Famous jali: <b>Sidi Saiyyed Mosque, Ahmedabad</b> (\"Tree of Life\" jali, 1573).<br>• <b>Salim Chishti's tomb</b> (Fatehpur Sikri) has fine marble jalis.<br>• Other Indo-Islamic features: <b>true arch, dome, minarets, pietra dura</b> and calligraphy.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – वायु-संचार और गोपनीयता प्रदान करते हुए प्रकाश को छानना</b><br><b>जालियाँ</b> (छिद्रित पत्थर की स्क्रीन) <b><u>सूर्य के प्रकाश को छानती थीं, वायु-संचार होने देती थीं और गोपनीयता देती थीं</u></b>, विशेषकर ज़नानखानों में; साथ ही ज्यामितीय और पुष्प आकृतियों से सुंदरता भी बढ़ाती थीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रसिद्ध जाली: <b>सीदी सैयद मस्जिद, अहमदाबाद</b> (\"जीवन वृक्ष\" जाली, 1573)।<br>• <b>सलीम चिश्ती का मकबरा</b> (फतेहपुर सीकरी) में संगमरमर की बारीक जालियाँ हैं।<br>• अन्य हिंद-इस्लामी विशेषताएँ: <b>वास्तविक मेहराब, गुंबद, मीनारें, पित्रा दुरा (Pietra dura)</b> और सुलेखन।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000070129","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Advent of Europeans","question":{"en":"Which of the following was not one of the principal reasons for Siraj-ud-Daula’s hostility towards the English East India Company in 1756? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"1756 में अंग्रेज़ी ईस्ट इंडिया कंपनी के प्रति सिराजुद्दौला की शत्रुता के प्रमुख कारणों में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा नहीं था? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Company fortified Calcutta without the Nawab’s permission.","hi":"कंपनी ने नवाब की अनुमति के बिना कलकत्ता की किलेबंदी की।"},"2":{"en":"The Company gave asylum to Krishna Das, the son of Raj Ballabh.","hi":"कंपनी ने राजबल्लभ के पुत्र कृष्णदास को शरण दी।"},"3":{"en":"The Company demanded the abolition of all inland duties on the salt trade.","hi":"कंपनी ने नमक व्यापार पर सभी आंतरिक शुल्कों को समाप्त करने की माँग की।"},"4":{"en":"The Company misused its trade privileges, causing financial losses to the Nawab.","hi":"कंपनी ने अपने व्यापारिक विशेषाधिकारों (दस्तक) का दुरुपयोग किया, जिससे नवाब को वित्तीय हानि हुई।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – The Company demanded the abolition of all inland duties on the salt trade.</b><br>Siraj-ud-Daula was angered by the <b>fortification of Calcutta</b>, the <b>asylum given to Krishna Das</b> and the <b>misuse of dastaks</b>. A demand to <b><u>abolish all inland duties on salt</u></b> was not among these causes.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Siraj captured Calcutta in <b>June 1756</b>; the <b>\"Black Hole Tragedy\"</b> is linked to this event.<br>• <b>Battle of Plassey</b> – <b>23 June 1757</b>; Robert Clive defeated Siraj with the help of <b>Mir Jafar</b>.<br>• <b>Battle of Buxar (1764)</b> led to the <b>Treaty of Allahabad (1765)</b> and Diwani rights.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – कंपनी ने नमक व्यापार पर सभी आंतरिक शुल्कों को समाप्त करने की माँग की।</b><br>सिराजुद्दौला <b>कलकत्ता की किलेबंदी</b>, <b>कृष्णदास को शरण</b> और <b>दस्तकों के दुरुपयोग</b> से नाराज़ था। <b><u>नमक पर सभी आंतरिक शुल्क समाप्त करने</u></b> की माँग इन कारणों में नहीं थी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सिराज ने <b>जून 1756</b> में कलकत्ता पर कब्ज़ा किया; <b>\"ब्लैक होल त्रासदी\"</b> इसी घटना से जुड़ी है।<br>• <b>प्लासी का युद्ध</b> – <b>23 जून 1757</b>; रॉबर्ट क्लाइव ने <b>मीर जाफ़र</b> की सहायता से सिराज को हराया।<br>• <b>बक्सर का युद्ध (1764)</b> के बाद <b>इलाहाबाद की संधि (1765)</b> और दीवानी अधिकार मिले।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000070130","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Circulatory System and Excretory System","question":{"en":"During physical exercise, a person’s pulse rate rises from 70 beats per minute to 110 beats per minute. By how many beats per minute does the pulse rate increase? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"शारीरिक व्यायाम के दौरान किसी व्यक्ति की नाड़ी दर 70 धड़कन प्रति मिनट से बढ़कर 110 धड़कन प्रति मिनट हो जाती है। नाड़ी दर में कितनी धड़कन प्रति मिनट की वृद्धि होती है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20 beats per minute","hi":"20 धड़कन प्रति मिनट"},"2":{"en":"30 beats per minute","hi":"30 धड़कन प्रति मिनट"},"3":{"en":"40 beats per minute","hi":"40 धड़कन प्रति मिनट"},"4":{"en":"50 beats per minute","hi":"50 धड़कन प्रति मिनट"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 40 beats per minute</b><br>Increase in pulse rate = 110 − 70 = <b><u>40 beats per minute</u></b>. During exercise the heart beats faster to supply more oxygen to the muscles.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Normal resting pulse rate of an adult: <b>60–100 beats/min</b> (average about 72).<br>• Pulse is usually felt at the <b>radial artery</b> (wrist).<br>• The heartbeat is initiated by the <b>SA node</b>, called the <b>pacemaker</b> of the heart.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 40 धड़कन प्रति मिनट</b><br>नाड़ी दर में वृद्धि = 110 − 70 = <b><u>40 धड़कन प्रति मिनट</u></b>। व्यायाम के दौरान मांसपेशियों को अधिक ऑक्सीजन पहुँचाने के लिए हृदय तेज़ी से धड़कता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वयस्क की सामान्य विश्राम नाड़ी दर: <b>60–100 धड़कन/मिनट</b> (औसत लगभग 72)।<br>• नाड़ी सामान्यतः <b>रेडियल धमनी (Radial artery)</b> (कलाई) पर महसूस की जाती है।<br>• हृदय की धड़कन <b>SA नोड</b> से शुरू होती है, जिसे हृदय का <b>पेसमेकर</b> कहते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000070131","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"If the volume of the sphere is \\(697\\frac{4}{21}\\) cm³ then find the radius of the sphere. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि गोले का आयतन \\(697\\frac{4}{21}\\) cm³ है, तो गोले की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6.5 cm"},"2":{"en":"5.8 cm"},"3":{"en":"5.5 cm"},"4":{"en":"4.5 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3 = \\frac{14641}{21}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{4}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} r^3 = \\frac{14641}{21} \\Rightarrow \\frac{88}{21}r^3 = \\frac{14641}{21}\\)<br>\\(r^3 = \\frac{14641}{88} = 166.375 \\Rightarrow r = 5.5\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{5.5\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 5.5 cm.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3 = \\frac{14641}{21}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{4}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} r^3 = \\frac{14641}{21} \\Rightarrow \\frac{88}{21}r^3 = \\frac{14641}{21}\\)<br>\\(r^3 = \\frac{14641}{88} = 166.375 \\Rightarrow r = 5.5\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{5.5\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 5.5 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000070132","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The sides of a triangle are in the ratio 4:7:7. If the perimeter is 90 cm, what is the area of the triangle? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक त्रिभुज की भुजाएँ 4:7:7 के अनुपात में हैं। यदि परिमाप 90 cm है, तो त्रिभुज का क्षेत्रफल क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(150\\sqrt{5}\\) cm²"},"2":{"en":"\\(250\\sqrt{5}\\) cm²"},"3":{"en":"\\(350\\sqrt{5}\\) cm²"},"4":{"en":"\\(9\\sqrt{5}\\) cm²"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(4k + 7k + 7k = 90 \\Rightarrow k = 5\\), sides are 20, 35, 35 cm (isosceles)<br>Height on the base 20: \\(\\sqrt{35^2 - 10^2} = \\sqrt{1125} = 15\\sqrt{5}\\)<br>Area \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 20 \\times 15\\sqrt{5} = \\boxed{150\\sqrt{5}\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(150\\sqrt{5}\\) cm².</b>","hi":"\\(4k + 7k + 7k = 90 \\Rightarrow k = 5\\), भुजाएँ 20, 35, 35 cm (समद्विबाहु)<br>आधार 20 पर ऊँचाई: \\(\\sqrt{35^2 - 10^2} = \\sqrt{1125} = 15\\sqrt{5}\\)<br>क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 20 \\times 15\\sqrt{5} = \\boxed{150\\sqrt{5}\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(150\\sqrt{5}\\) cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000070133","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Congruent triangles are joined to form a six-sided polygon in which all sides are equal and each interior angle is obtuse. How would you classify this polygon? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"सर्वांगसम त्रिभुजों को जोड़कर एक छह-भुजीय बहुभुज बनाया जाता है जिसमें सभी भुजाएँ बराबर हैं और प्रत्येक अंतःकोण अधिक कोण है। आप इस बहुभुज को कैसे वर्गीकृत करेंगे? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Regular octagon","hi":"सम अष्टभुज"},"2":{"en":"Regular decagon","hi":"सम दशभुज"},"3":{"en":"Regular hexagon","hi":"सम षट्भुज"},"4":{"en":"Regular pentagon","hi":"सम पंचभुज"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A polygon with six equal sides and all interior angles equal (and obtuse, each \\(120°\\))<br>Interior angle \\(= \\frac{(6 - 2) \\times 180°}{6} = 120°\\)<br>It is a \\(\\boxed{\\text{Regular hexagon}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Regular hexagon.</b>","hi":"छह बराबर भुजाओं और सभी अंतःकोण बराबर (तथा अधिक, प्रत्येक \\(120°\\)) वाला बहुभुज<br>अंतःकोण \\(= \\frac{(6 - 2) \\times 180°}{6} = 120°\\)<br>यह \\(\\boxed{\\text{सम षट्भुज}}\\) है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): सम षट्भुज है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000070134","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Examine the frequency polygon on math Exam Scores (out of 100), Groups: Batch A vs. Batch B and answer the following question.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/0197f7b4-ec05-717b-afa5-13203e5239a0_EN.jpg?edu=639294370242169194\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>In the frequency polygon comparison of Batch A and Batch B, at which score interval is the difference in frequencies between the two batches the greatest? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"गणित की परीक्षा के अंकों (100 में से) पर बारंबारता बहुभुज देखिए, समूह: बैच A बनाम बैच B, और निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/0197f7b4-ec05-717b-afa5-13203e5239a0_HI.jpg?edu=639294370368113237\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>बैच A और बैच B की बारंबारता बहुभुज तुलना में किस अंक अंतराल पर दोनों बैचों की बारंबारताओं का अंतर सबसे अधिक है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0 – 20"},"2":{"en":"20 – 40"},"3":{"en":"80 – 100"},"4":{"en":"40 – 60"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"From the polygon: Batch A = 5, 12, 25, 18, 10 and Batch B = 10, 18, 22, 15, 5<br>Differences: \\(|5 - 10| = 5\\), \\(|12 - 18| = 6\\), \\(|25 - 22| = 3\\), \\(|18 - 15| = 3\\), \\(|10 - 5| = 5\\)<br>The greatest difference is 6, in the interval \\(\\boxed{20\\text{–}40}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 20 – 40.</b>","hi":"बहुभुज से: बैच A = 5, 12, 25, 18, 10 और बैच B = 10, 18, 22, 15, 5<br>अंतर: \\(|5 - 10| = 5\\), \\(|12 - 18| = 6\\), \\(|25 - 22| = 3\\), \\(|18 - 15| = 3\\), \\(|10 - 5| = 5\\)<br>सबसे अधिक अंतर 6 है, अंतराल \\(\\boxed{20\\text{–}40}\\) में<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 20 – 40 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/0197f7b4-ec05-717b-afa5-13203e5239a0_EN.jpg?edu=639294370242169194","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/0197f7b4-ec05-717b-afa5-13203e5239a0_HI.jpg?edu=639294370368113237"]}},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000070135","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If sin A = 3/5 and A is acute, find the value of (1 + tan²A) / sec²A. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि sin A = 3/5 और A न्यून कोण है, तो (1 + tan²A) / sec²A का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"9/16"},"3":{"en":"25/16"},"4":{"en":"4/3"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(1 + \\tan^2 A = \\sec^2 A\\) is an identity<br>So \\(\\frac{1 + \\tan^2 A}{\\sec^2 A} = \\frac{\\sec^2 A}{\\sec^2 A}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"\\(1 + \\tan^2 A = \\sec^2 A\\) एक सर्वसमिका है<br>अतः \\(\\frac{1 + \\tan^2 A}{\\sec^2 A} = \\frac{\\sec^2 A}{\\sec^2 A}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000070136","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"If in a circle with center O, two chords PQ & RS are equal such that ∠POQ = 70° & ∠ORS = p°. Calculate 3p° - 50°. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि केंद्र O वाले एक वृत्त में दो जीवाएँ PQ और RS इस प्रकार बराबर हैं कि ∠POQ = 70° और ∠ORS = p° है। 3p° - 50° की गणना कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"105°"},"2":{"en":"115°"},"3":{"en":"125°"},"4":{"en":"135°"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Equal chords subtend equal angles at the centre, so \\(\\angle ROS = 70°\\)<br>In isosceles \\(\\triangle ORS\\), \\(\\angle ORS = \\frac{180° - 70°}{2} = 55°\\), so \\(p = 55\\)<br>\\(3p - 50 = 165 - 50 = \\boxed{115°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 115°.</b>","hi":"बराबर जीवाएँ केंद्र पर बराबर कोण अंतरित करती हैं, अतः \\(\\angle ROS = 70°\\)<br>समद्विबाहु \\(\\triangle ORS\\) में \\(\\angle ORS = \\frac{180° - 70°}{2} = 55°\\), अतः \\(p = 55\\)<br>\\(3p - 50 = 165 - 50 = \\boxed{115°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 115° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000070137","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"Using the provided bar graph, which shows the number of students in each class, answer the following questions.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/01980c48-7db8-7af9-b0e5-56eac41e4ccf_EN.jpg?edu=639294370242451009\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If Class IV is split into two sections with an equal number of students, and Class III merges with one of these sections, what percentage of the total students would be in that merged section? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिए गए बार ग्राफ का उपयोग कीजिए, जो प्रत्येक कक्षा के विद्यार्थियों की संख्या दर्शाता है, और निम्नलिखित प्रश्नों का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/01980c48-7db8-7af9-b0e5-56eac41e4ccf_HI.jpg?edu=639294370368329359\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि कक्षा IV को बराबर विद्यार्थियों वाले दो वर्गों में बाँटा जाए और कक्षा III उनमें से एक वर्ग में मिला दी जाए, तो उस मिले हुए वर्ग में कुल विद्यार्थियों का कितना प्रतिशत होगा? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30%"},"2":{"en":"32%"},"3":{"en":"34%"},"4":{"en":"36%"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"From the bar graph: Class I = 45, II = 50, III = 40, IV = 60, V = 40 (total \\(= 235\\))<br>Half of Class IV \\(= 30\\); merged section \\(= 40 + 30 = 70\\)<br>Percentage \\(= \\frac{70}{235} \\times 100 \\approx 29.8\\% \\approx \\boxed{30\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 30%.</b>","hi":"बार ग्राफ से: कक्षा I = 45, II = 50, III = 40, IV = 60, V = 40 (कुल \\(= 235\\))<br>कक्षा IV का आधा \\(= 30\\); मिला हुआ वर्ग \\(= 40 + 30 = 70\\)<br>प्रतिशत \\(= \\frac{70}{235} \\times 100 \\approx 29.8\\% \\approx \\boxed{30\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 30% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/01980c48-7db8-7af9-b0e5-56eac41e4ccf_EN.jpg?edu=639294370242451009","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/01980c48-7db8-7af9-b0e5-56eac41e4ccf_HI.jpg?edu=639294370368329359"]}},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000070138","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"Examine the bar graph below, answer the following question.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/0198116c-ea9c-7535-ba48-1c2e1004f33b_EN.jpg?edu=639294370242577358\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>What is the total number of internet users across all five states, and what approximate percentage of them are urban users? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"नीचे दिए बार ग्राफ का अवलोकन कीजिए और निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/0198116c-ea9c-7535-ba48-1c2e1004f33b_HI.jpg?edu=639294370368421172\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>सभी पाँच राज्यों में इंटरनेट उपयोगकर्ताओं की कुल संख्या कितनी है और उनमें से लगभग कितने प्रतिशत शहरी उपयोगकर्ता हैं? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"309 million total; 61% urban","hi":"309 मिलियन कुल; 61% शहरी"},"2":{"en":"309 million total; 59% urban","hi":"309 मिलियन कुल; 59% शहरी"},"3":{"en":"314 million total; 60% urban","hi":"314 मिलियन कुल; 60% शहरी"},"4":{"en":"307 million total; 63% urban","hi":"307 मिलियन कुल; 63% शहरी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Urban: 40 + 50 + 35 + 25 + 38 = 188 million<br>Rural: 25 + 30 + 28 + 18 + 20 = 121 million<br>Total \\(= 188 + 121 = 309\\) million; urban % \\(= \\frac{188}{309} \\times 100 \\approx 60.8\\% \\approx 61\\%\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{309\\ \\text{million total; } 61\\%\\ \\text{urban}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 309 million total; 61% urban.</b>","hi":"शहरी: 40 + 50 + 35 + 25 + 38 = 188 मिलियन<br>ग्रामीण: 25 + 30 + 28 + 18 + 20 = 121 मिलियन<br>कुल \\(= 188 + 121 = 309\\) मिलियन; शहरी % \\(= \\frac{188}{309} \\times 100 \\approx 60.8\\% \\approx 61\\%\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{309\\ \\text{million total; } 61\\%\\ \\text{urban}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 309 मिलियन कुल; 61% शहरी है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/0198116c-ea9c-7535-ba48-1c2e1004f33b_EN.jpg?edu=639294370242577358","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/0198116c-ea9c-7535-ba48-1c2e1004f33b_HI.jpg?edu=639294370368421172"]}},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000070139","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"Carefully study the pie chart showing the distribution of favorite colors. Then answer the following questions.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/01981219-e319-7277-9c1d-714609d711c8_EN.jpg?edu=639294370242712907\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Which three categories combined account for the same percentage as Rent? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पसंदीदा रंगों के वितरण को दर्शाने वाले पाई चार्ट का ध्यानपूर्वक अध्ययन कीजिए। फिर निम्नलिखित प्रश्नों का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/01981219-e319-7277-9c1d-714609d711c8_HI.jpg?edu=639294370368529067\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>कौन-सी तीन श्रेणियाँ मिलकर Rent के बराबर प्रतिशत रखती हैं? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Utilities, Transportation, Entertainment"},"2":{"en":"Groceries, Entertainment, Savings"},"3":{"en":"Transportation, Entertainment, Savings"},"4":{"en":"Rent, Transportation, Savings"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"From the pie chart: Rent = 35%, Transportation = 10%, Entertainment = 10%, Savings = 15%<br>\\(10\\% + 10\\% + 15\\% = 35\\%\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\text{Transportation, Entertainment, Savings}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Transportation, Entertainment, Savings.</b>","hi":"पाई चार्ट से: Rent = 35%, Transportation = 10%, Entertainment = 10%, Savings = 15%<br>\\(10\\% + 10\\% + 15\\% = 35\\%\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\text{Transportation, Entertainment, Savings}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): Transportation, Entertainment, Savings है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/01981219-e319-7277-9c1d-714609d711c8_EN.jpg?edu=639294370242712907","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/01981219-e319-7277-9c1d-714609d711c8_HI.jpg?edu=639294370368529067"]}},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000070140","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Examine the histogram showing how many employees fall within various salary ranges (in thousands of dollars). Use this data to answer the questions below.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/01981221-8e98-7576-ac48-7fbebe2e5436_EN.jpg?edu=639294370242868263\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Which of the following salary ranges has no employees? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यह आयतचित्र देखिए जो दर्शाता है कि कितने कर्मचारी विभिन्न वेतन श्रेणियों (हज़ार डॉलर में) में आते हैं। नीचे दिए प्रश्नों का उत्तर देने के लिए इस आँकड़े का उपयोग कीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/01981221-8e98-7576-ac48-7fbebe2e5436_HI.jpg?edu=639294370368643004\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>निम्नलिखित में से किस वेतन श्रेणी में कोई कर्मचारी नहीं है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"80–90 thousand","hi":"80–90 हज़ार"},"2":{"en":"0–10 thousand","hi":"0–10 हज़ार"},"3":{"en":"90–100 thousand","hi":"90–100 हज़ार"},"4":{"en":"60–70 thousand","hi":"60–70 हज़ार"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"From the histogram the frequencies are 100, 200, 200, 300, 450, 400, 300, 200, 100 and then 0<br>The bar for 90–100 is flat, so no employees lie there<br>\\(= \\boxed{90\\text{–}100\\ \\text{thousand}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 90–100 thousand.</b>","hi":"आयतचित्र से बारंबारताएँ 100, 200, 200, 300, 450, 400, 300, 200, 100 और फिर 0 हैं<br>90–100 का स्तंभ शून्य है, अतः वहाँ कोई कर्मचारी नहीं है<br>\\(= \\boxed{90\\text{–}100\\ \\text{thousand}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 90–100 हज़ार है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/01981221-8e98-7576-ac48-7fbebe2e5436_EN.jpg?edu=639294370242868263","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/01981221-8e98-7576-ac48-7fbebe2e5436_HI.jpg?edu=639294370368643004"]}},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000070141","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"A student was asked to multiply a number by 5/9, but instead, he divided it by 5/9. If his answer was 56 more than the correct answer, find the number. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक विद्यार्थी से किसी संख्या को 5/9 से गुणा करने को कहा गया, परंतु उसने उसे 5/9 से भाग दे दिया। यदि उसका उत्तर सही उत्तर से 56 अधिक था, तो संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"54"},"2":{"en":"45"},"3":{"en":"76"},"4":{"en":"85"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let the number be \\(x\\)<br>\\(\\frac{9x}{5} - \\frac{5x}{9} = 56 \\Rightarrow \\frac{81x - 25x}{45} = 56\\)<br>\\(\\frac{56x}{45} = 56 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{45}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 45.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए संख्या \\(x\\) है<br>\\(\\frac{9x}{5} - \\frac{5x}{9} = 56 \\Rightarrow \\frac{81x - 25x}{45} = 56\\)<br>\\(\\frac{56x}{45} = 56 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{45}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 45 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000070142","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the value of K if \\(\\frac{(0.9)^6 - (0.4)^6}{(0.9)^4 + 0.1296 + (0.4)^4} = K\\). [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"K का मान ज्ञात कीजिए यदि \\(\\frac{(0.9)^6 - (0.4)^6}{(0.9)^4 + 0.1296 + (0.4)^4} = K\\) है। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.35"},"2":{"en":"0.45"},"3":{"en":"0.25"},"4":{"en":"0.65"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Put \\(a = 0.9^2 = 0.81\\) and \\(b = 0.4^2 = 0.16\\); then \\(0.1296 = ab\\)<br>So the expression is \\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2}\\)<br>\\(a^3 - b^3 = (a - b)(a^2 + ab + b^2) \\Rightarrow K = a - b\\)<br>\\(K = 0.81 - 0.16 = \\boxed{0.65}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 0.65.</b>","hi":"\\(a = 0.9^2 = 0.81\\) और \\(b = 0.4^2 = 0.16\\) रखिए; तब \\(0.1296 = ab\\)<br>अतः व्यंजक \\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2}\\) बन जाता है<br>\\(a^3 - b^3 = (a - b)(a^2 + ab + b^2) \\Rightarrow K = a - b\\)<br>\\(K = 0.81 - 0.16 = \\boxed{0.65}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 0.65 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000070143","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the remainder when (6.8³ - 0.008) is divided by (6.8² + 1.36 + 0.04). [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"(6.8³ - 0.008) को (6.8² + 1.36 + 0.04) से भाग देने पर शेषफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"0"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"5"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Here \\(1.36 = 6.8 \\times 0.2\\) and \\(0.008 = 0.2^3\\), so the divisor is \\(a^2 + ab + b^2\\) and the dividend is \\(a^3 - b^3\\)<br>\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\) exactly, so the remainder is 0<br>\\(= \\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 0.</b>","hi":"यहाँ \\(1.36 = 6.8 \\times 0.2\\) और \\(0.008 = 0.2^3\\), अतः भाजक \\(a^2 + ab + b^2\\) और भाज्य \\(a^3 - b^3\\) है<br>\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\) ठीक-ठीक, अतः शेषफल 0 है<br>\\(= \\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 0 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000070144","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"Find the mean proportional between 0.81 and 4.41. (Round off to one decimal place.) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"0.81 और 4.41 के बीच माध्य समानुपाती ज्ञात कीजिए। (एक दशमलव स्थान तक पूर्णांकित कीजिए।) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2.1"},"2":{"en":"3.6"},"3":{"en":"4.7"},"4":{"en":"1.9"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Mean proportional \\(= \\sqrt{0.81 \\times 4.41}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{3.5721}\\)<br>\\(= 1.89 \\approx \\boxed{1.9}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 1.9.</b>","hi":"माध्य समानुपाती \\(= \\sqrt{0.81 \\times 4.41}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{3.5721}\\)<br>\\(= 1.89 \\approx \\boxed{1.9}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 1.9 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000070145","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"An item is sold at 25% profit. If the cost price decreases by 10% and the selling price also decreases by 10%, the new profit percentage will be: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वस्तु 25% लाभ पर बेची जाती है। यदि क्रय मूल्य 10% घट जाए और विक्रय मूल्य भी 10% घट जाए, तो नया लाभ प्रतिशत होगा: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45%"},"2":{"en":"25%"},"3":{"en":"35%"},"4":{"en":"65%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let CP \\(= 100\\), SP \\(= 125\\)<br>New CP \\(= 90\\), new SP \\(= 112.5\\)<br>Profit \\(= \\frac{22.5}{90} \\times 100 = \\boxed{25\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 25%.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए क्रय मूल्य \\(= 100\\), विक्रय मूल्य \\(= 125\\)<br>नया क्रय मूल्य \\(= 90\\), नया विक्रय मूल्य \\(= 112.5\\)<br>लाभ \\(= \\frac{22.5}{90} \\times 100 = \\boxed{25\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 25% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000070146","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In △PQR, I is a point which is equidistant from all the sides of a Δ. If ∠PRQ = 30°, then find ∠QIR + ∠PIR. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"△PQR में, I एक ऐसा बिंदु है जो त्रिभुज की सभी भुजाओं से समान दूरी पर है। यदि ∠PRQ = 30° है, तो ∠QIR + ∠PIR ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"275°"},"2":{"en":"225°"},"3":{"en":"295°"},"4":{"en":"255°"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"I is the incentre, so \\(\\angle QIR = 90° + \\frac{\\angle P}{2}\\) and \\(\\angle PIR = 90° + \\frac{\\angle Q}{2}\\)<br>Sum \\(= 180° + \\frac{\\angle P + \\angle Q}{2} = 180° + \\frac{180° - 30°}{2}\\)<br>\\(= 180° + 75° = \\boxed{255°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 255°.</b>","hi":"I अंतःकेंद्र है, अतः \\(\\angle QIR = 90° + \\frac{\\angle P}{2}\\) और \\(\\angle PIR = 90° + \\frac{\\angle Q}{2}\\)<br>योग \\(= 180° + \\frac{\\angle P + \\angle Q}{2} = 180° + \\frac{180° - 30°}{2}\\)<br>\\(= 180° + 75° = \\boxed{255°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 255° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000070147","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"The angle of elevation of the top of a tower from two points at distances a and b from the base of the tower and in the same straight line with it are 30° and 60° respectively. If the height of the tower is h, find h in terms of b. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"मीनार के आधार से a और b दूरी पर तथा उसी सीधी रेखा में स्थित दो बिंदुओं से मीनार के शिखर के उन्नयन कोण क्रमशः 30° और 60° हैं। यदि मीनार की ऊँचाई h है, तो h को b के पदों में ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(h = b\\sqrt{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(b = h\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(h \\times b = \\sqrt{3}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(h = b\\sqrt{3}\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"From the nearer point (distance b): \\(\\tan 60° = \\frac{h}{b}\\)<br>\\(h = b\\tan 60° = b\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{h = b\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(h = b\\sqrt{3}\\).</b>","hi":"निकट बिंदु (दूरी b) से: \\(\\tan 60° = \\frac{h}{b}\\)<br>\\(h = b\\tan 60° = b\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{h = b\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(h = b\\sqrt{3}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000070148","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A square lawn is enclosed by a path of uniform width 2.5 m. Given that the area of the path is 165 m², determine the side length of the square lawn. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वर्गाकार लॉन के चारों ओर 2.5 m एकसमान चौड़ाई का पथ है। यदि पथ का क्षेत्रफल 165 m² है, तो वर्गाकार लॉन की भुजा की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12 m"},"2":{"en":"14 m"},"3":{"en":"17 m"},"4":{"en":"19 m"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let the side of the lawn be \\(s\\)<br>Path area \\(= (s + 5)^2 - s^2 = 10s + 25 = 165\\)<br>\\(10s = 140 \\Rightarrow s = \\boxed{14\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 14 m.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए लॉन की भुजा \\(s\\) है<br>पथ का क्षेत्रफल \\(= (s + 5)^2 - s^2 = 10s + 25 = 165\\)<br>\\(10s = 140 \\Rightarrow s = \\boxed{14\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 14 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000070149","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In a circle, chord AB subtends an angle of 42° at point P on the circumference. Find the angle subtended by the same chord at another point Q lying on the same segment. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वृत्त में जीवा AB परिधि पर स्थित बिंदु P पर 42° का कोण अंतरित करती है। उसी जीवा द्वारा उसी वृत्तखंड में स्थित दूसरे बिंदु Q पर अंतरित कोण ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"21°"},"2":{"en":"42°"},"3":{"en":"69°"},"4":{"en":"111°"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Angles subtended by the same chord in the same segment are equal<br>So the angle at Q is also \\(\\boxed{42°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 42°.</b>","hi":"एक ही वृत्तखंड में एक ही जीवा द्वारा अंतरित कोण बराबर होते हैं<br>अतः Q पर कोण भी \\(\\boxed{42°}\\) है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 42° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000070150","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In two congruent right-angled triangles ABC and PQR, angles A and P are 90°. If BC = 15 cm and PR = 9 cm, find AB. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दो सर्वांगसम समकोण त्रिभुजों ABC और PQR में कोण A और P = 90° हैं। यदि BC = 15 cm और PR = 9 cm है, तो AB ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15 cm"},"2":{"en":"12 cm"},"3":{"en":"9 cm"},"4":{"en":"6 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Congruent triangles give \\(AB = PQ\\) and \\(AC = PR = 9\\) cm, with hypotenuse \\(BC = 15\\) cm<br>\\(AB = \\sqrt{15^2 - 9^2} = \\sqrt{144}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{12\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 12 cm.</b>","hi":"सर्वांगसम त्रिभुजों से \\(AB = PQ\\) और \\(AC = PR = 9\\) cm, कर्ण \\(BC = 15\\) cm<br>\\(AB = \\sqrt{15^2 - 9^2} = \\sqrt{144}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{12\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 12 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000070151","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two circles of radii 13 cm and 15 cm intersect, and the distance between their centers is 14 cm. Find the length of their common chord. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"13 cm और 15 cm त्रिज्या वाले दो वृत्त प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं और उनके केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी 14 cm है। उनकी उभयनिष्ठ जीवा की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 cm"},"2":{"en":"12 cm"},"3":{"en":"17 cm"},"4":{"en":"24 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let the common chord cut the line of centres at distance \\(x\\) from the first centre<br>\\(13^2 - x^2 = 15^2 - (14 - x)^2\\)<br>\\(169 - x^2 = 225 - 196 + 28x - x^2 \\Rightarrow 28x = 140 \\Rightarrow x = 5\\)<br>Half chord \\(= \\sqrt{169 - 25} = 12\\), so chord \\(= \\boxed{24\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 24 cm.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए उभयनिष्ठ जीवा केंद्र रेखा को पहले केंद्र से \\(x\\) दूरी पर काटती है<br>\\(13^2 - x^2 = 15^2 - (14 - x)^2\\)<br>\\(169 - x^2 = 225 - 196 + 28x - x^2 \\Rightarrow 28x = 140 \\Rightarrow x = 5\\)<br>आधी जीवा \\(= \\sqrt{169 - 25} = 12\\), अतः जीवा \\(= \\boxed{24\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 24 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000070152","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A merchant has a total of 1000 kg of sugar. He sells part of it at a profit of 8% and the remaining at a profit of 18%. If his overall profit is 14%, how much of the sugar was sold at 18% profit? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक व्यापारी के पास कुल 1000 kg चीनी है। वह इसका एक भाग 8% लाभ पर और शेष 18% लाभ पर बेचता है। यदि उसका कुल लाभ 14% है, तो 18% लाभ पर कितनी चीनी बेची गई? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"400 kg"},"2":{"en":"560 kg"},"3":{"en":"600 kg"},"4":{"en":"640 kg"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"By alligation: \\(8\\%\\) and \\(18\\%\\) give a mean of \\(14\\%\\)<br>Ratio \\(= (18 - 14) : (14 - 8) = 4 : 6 = 2 : 3\\)<br>Quantity at 18% profit \\(= \\frac{3}{5} \\times 1000 = \\boxed{600\\ \\text{kg}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 600 kg.</b>","hi":"मिश्रण नियम से: \\(8\\%\\) और \\(18\\%\\) का माध्य \\(14\\%\\) है<br>अनुपात \\(= (18 - 14) : (14 - 8) = 4 : 6 = 2 : 3\\)<br>18% लाभ पर मात्रा \\(= \\frac{3}{5} \\times 1000 = \\boxed{600\\ \\text{kg}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 600 kg है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000070153","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two circles have radii 8 cm and 5 cm. If the length of their transverse common tangent is 16 cm, find the distance between their centers (in cm). [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दो वृत्तों की त्रिज्याएँ 8 cm और 5 cm हैं। यदि उनकी तिर्यक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा की लंबाई 16 cm है, तो उनके केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी (cm में) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(5\\sqrt{17}\\) cm"},"2":{"en":"\\(7\\sqrt{13}\\) cm"},"3":{"en":"9 cm"},"4":{"en":"18 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Transverse common tangent \\(= \\sqrt{d^2 - (r_1 + r_2)^2}\\)<br>\\(16 = \\sqrt{d^2 - 13^2} \\Rightarrow d^2 = 256 + 169 = 425\\)<br>\\(d = \\sqrt{425} = 5\\sqrt{17}\\) cm \\(= \\boxed{5\\sqrt{17}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(5\\sqrt{17}\\) cm.</b>","hi":"तिर्यक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा \\(= \\sqrt{d^2 - (r_1 + r_2)^2}\\)<br>\\(16 = \\sqrt{d^2 - 13^2} \\Rightarrow d^2 = 256 + 169 = 425\\)<br>\\(d = \\sqrt{425} = 5\\sqrt{17}\\) cm \\(= \\boxed{5\\sqrt{17}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(5\\sqrt{17}\\) cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000070154","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"The following pie-chart shows the percentage distribution of energy consumption from various sources. Study the pie-chart carefully and answer the question based on it.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/019e6d85-eb0e-7a75-a875-e3cf5e1f2522_EN.jpg?edu=639294370246629085\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>The total energy consumed is 10,000 units. The contribution from 'Coal' is reduced by one-fifth of its current amount. To keep the total energy consumption unchanged, the usage of 'Natural Gas' must be increased. Determine the percentage by which 'Natural Gas' consumption should be raised to compensate for the reduction in 'Coal'. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित पाई-चार्ट विभिन्न स्रोतों से ऊर्जा खपत के प्रतिशत वितरण को दर्शाता है। पाई-चार्ट का ध्यानपूर्वक अध्ययन कीजिए और उसके आधार पर प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/019e6d85-eb0e-7a75-a875-e3cf5e1f2522_HI.jpg?edu=639294370371406627\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>कुल खपत की गई ऊर्जा 10,000 इकाई है। 'Coal' का योगदान उसकी वर्तमान मात्रा के पाँचवें भाग से घटा दिया जाता है। कुल ऊर्जा खपत अपरिवर्तित रखने के लिए 'Natural Gas' का उपयोग बढ़ाना होगा। 'Coal' में कमी की भरपाई के लिए 'Natural Gas' की खपत कितने प्रतिशत बढ़ानी होगी? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45%"},"2":{"en":"40%"},"3":{"en":"30%"},"4":{"en":"35%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"From the pie chart: Coal \\(= 30\\%\\), Natural Gas \\(= 20\\%\\)<br>Total \\(= 10{,}000\\) units, so Coal \\(= 3000\\) units and Natural Gas \\(= 2000\\) units<br>Coal reduced by one-fifth \\(= \\frac{3000}{5} = 600\\) units<br>Natural Gas must rise from 2000 to 2600, i.e. by \\(\\frac{600}{2000} \\times 100 = \\boxed{30\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 30%.</b>","hi":"पाई चार्ट से: Coal \\(= 30\\%\\), Natural Gas \\(= 20\\%\\)<br>कुल \\(= 10{,}000\\) इकाई, अतः Coal \\(= 3000\\) और Natural Gas \\(= 2000\\) इकाई<br>कोयले में एक-पाँचवांश कमी \\(= \\frac{3000}{5} = 600\\) इकाई<br>नैजरल गैस को 2000 से 2600 तक बढ़ाना होगा, अर्थात् \\(\\frac{600}{2000} \\times 100 = \\boxed{30\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 30% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/EN/019e6d85-eb0e-7a75-a875-e3cf5e1f2522_EN.jpg?edu=639294370246629085","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct1/qimg/3/HI/019e6d85-eb0e-7a75-a875-e3cf5e1f2522_HI.jpg?edu=639294370371406627"]}},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000070155","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"In a corporate shareholder election, 60% of the voters were male, and the rest were female. 40% of the male voters and 70% of the female voters voted for Proposal A. If the total number of voters who did not vote for Proposal A is 1,200, find the total number of shareholders who cast a vote. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक कॉर्पोरेट शेयरधारक चुनाव में 60% मतदाता पुरुष थे और शेष महिलाएँ। 40% पुरुष मतदाताओं और 70% महिला मतदाताओं ने प्रस्ताव A के पक्ष में मत दिया। यदि प्रस्ताव A के पक्ष में मत न देने वाले मतदाताओं की कुल संख्या 1,200 है, तो मतदान करने वाले शेयरधारकों की कुल संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2,400"},"2":{"en":"2,500"},"3":{"en":"2,600"},"4":{"en":"2,800"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let total voters be \\(N\\); males \\(= 0.6N\\), females \\(= 0.4N\\)<br>Not voting for A: \\(0.6(0.6N) + 0.3(0.4N) = 0.36N + 0.12N = 0.48N\\)<br>\\(0.48N = 1200 \\Rightarrow N = \\boxed{2500}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2,500.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए कुल मतदाता \\(N\\) हैं; पुरुष \\(= 0.6N\\), महिलाएँ \\(= 0.4N\\)<br>A के पक्ष में मत न देने वाले: \\(0.6(0.6N) + 0.3(0.4N) = 0.36N + 0.12N = 0.48N\\)<br>\\(0.48N = 1200 \\Rightarrow N = \\boxed{2500}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2,500 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000070156","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5).<br>Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>Once a revered ritual, letter writing has steadily <b>(1)</b> ____ into a relic of bygone eras, displaced by the relentless immediacy of digital communication. There was a time when a single envelope, ink-smudged and weatherworn, <b>(2)</b> ____ profound intimacies across continents, preserving sentiments too sacred to entrust to fleeting conversations. Today’s sterile texts and hastily composed emails seldom replicate the tactility that imbued handwritten letters with gravitas; every flourish, every hesitant stroke, bore the <b>(3) vestiges</b> of a soul laid bare. It is not merely nostalgia that compels some to cling to this endangered practice, but recognition that certain articulations of the heart <b>(4)</b> ___ better when filtered through the slowness of ink and parchment. Indeed, the act of penning a letter demands a kind of <b>(5) deliberateness</b> rare in an age characterized by impulsivity and ephemerality. Though the world races ever forward, perhaps in the margins of our modern lives, the art of letter-writing will preserve a fragile thread tethering us to a slower, richer past.<br><br><br>Choose correct tense.(1) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"diminish"},"2":{"en":"diminished"},"3":{"en":"diminishing"},"4":{"en":"had diminished"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…letter writing has steadily (1) ____ into a relic of bygone eras…\"</i><br>Grammar: 'has' + adverb 'steadily' needs the past participle (V3) to form the present perfect.<br>Meaning: <b>diminished (घटकर रह गया)</b> – letter writing has shrunk into a relic.<br>diminish – base form cannot follow 'has'<br>diminishing – 'has diminishing' is ungrammatical<br>had diminished – 'has had diminished' is impossible<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): diminished.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000070157","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5).<br>Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>Once a revered ritual, letter writing has steadily <b>(1)</b> ____ into a relic of bygone eras, displaced by the relentless immediacy of digital communication. There was a time when a single envelope, ink-smudged and weatherworn, <b>(2)</b> ____ profound intimacies across continents, preserving sentiments too sacred to entrust to fleeting conversations. Today’s sterile texts and hastily composed emails seldom replicate the tactility that imbued handwritten letters with gravitas; every flourish, every hesitant stroke, bore the <b>(3) vestiges</b> of a soul laid bare. It is not merely nostalgia that compels some to cling to this endangered practice, but recognition that certain articulations of the heart <b>(4)</b> ___ better when filtered through the slowness of ink and parchment. Indeed, the act of penning a letter demands a kind of <b>(5) deliberateness</b> rare in an age characterized by impulsivity and ephemerality. Though the world races ever forward, perhaps in the margins of our modern lives, the art of letter-writing will preserve a fragile thread tethering us to a slower, richer past.<br><br><br>Choose correct verb form.(2) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"convey"},"2":{"en":"conveying"},"3":{"en":"conveyed"},"4":{"en":"had conveying"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<i>\"There was a time when a single envelope … (2) ____ profound intimacies across continents…\"</i><br>Grammar: 'There was a time when' refers to the past, and the singular subject 'a single envelope' needs a finite past verb.<br>Meaning: <b>conveyed (पहुँचाया)</b> – the envelope carried deep feelings.<br>convey – present form does not suit the past time<br>conveying – not a finite verb<br>had conveying – ungrammatical<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): conveyed.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000070158","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5).<br>Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>Once a revered ritual, letter writing has steadily <b>(1)</b> ____ into a relic of bygone eras, displaced by the relentless immediacy of digital communication. There was a time when a single envelope, ink-smudged and weatherworn, <b>(2)</b> ____ profound intimacies across continents, preserving sentiments too sacred to entrust to fleeting conversations. Today’s sterile texts and hastily composed emails seldom replicate the tactility that imbued handwritten letters with gravitas; every flourish, every hesitant stroke, bore the <b>(3) vestiges</b> of a soul laid bare. It is not merely nostalgia that compels some to cling to this endangered practice, but recognition that certain articulations of the heart <b>(4)</b> ___ better when filtered through the slowness of ink and parchment. Indeed, the act of penning a letter demands a kind of <b>(5) deliberateness</b> rare in an age characterized by impulsivity and ephemerality. Though the world races ever forward, perhaps in the margins of our modern lives, the art of letter-writing will preserve a fragile thread tethering us to a slower, richer past.<br><br><br>The word “vestiges” most nearly means: (3) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Polished embellishments"},"2":{"en":"Remaining traces"},"3":{"en":"Heavy burdens"},"4":{"en":"Concealed meanings"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…every flourish, every hesitant stroke, bore the (3) vestiges of a soul laid bare.\"</i><br><b>Vestiges (अवशेष, निशान)</b> = small remaining traces of something.<br>Each stroke of the pen carried traces of the writer's soul.<br>Polished embellishments (सजावट) – decoration, not traces<br>Heavy burdens (भारी बोझ) – unrelated<br>Concealed meanings (छिपे अर्थ) – the soul is 'laid bare', not hidden<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Remaining traces.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000070159","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5).<br>Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>Once a revered ritual, letter writing has steadily <b>(1)</b> ____ into a relic of bygone eras, displaced by the relentless immediacy of digital communication. There was a time when a single envelope, ink-smudged and weatherworn, <b>(2)</b> ____ profound intimacies across continents, preserving sentiments too sacred to entrust to fleeting conversations. Today’s sterile texts and hastily composed emails seldom replicate the tactility that imbued handwritten letters with gravitas; every flourish, every hesitant stroke, bore the <b>(3) vestiges</b> of a soul laid bare. It is not merely nostalgia that compels some to cling to this endangered practice, but recognition that certain articulations of the heart <b>(4)</b> ___ better when filtered through the slowness of ink and parchment. Indeed, the act of penning a letter demands a kind of <b>(5) deliberateness</b> rare in an age characterized by impulsivity and ephemerality. Though the world races ever forward, perhaps in the margins of our modern lives, the art of letter-writing will preserve a fragile thread tethering us to a slower, richer past.<br><br><br>Choose correct tense.(4) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"transpires"},"2":{"en":"have transpired"},"3":{"en":"transpire"},"4":{"en":"transpired"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…recognition that certain articulations of the heart (4) ___ better when filtered through the slowness of ink…\"</i><br>Grammar: the subject 'articulations' is plural and the statement is a general truth, so the simple present plural form is needed.<br>Meaning: <b>transpire (प्रकट होना)</b> = come out, become known.<br>transpires – singular verb with plural subject<br>have transpired – present perfect does not suit a general truth<br>transpired – past tense; the passage speaks of the present<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): transpire.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000070160","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5).<br>Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>Once a revered ritual, letter writing has steadily <b>(1)</b> ____ into a relic of bygone eras, displaced by the relentless immediacy of digital communication. There was a time when a single envelope, ink-smudged and weatherworn, <b>(2)</b> ____ profound intimacies across continents, preserving sentiments too sacred to entrust to fleeting conversations. Today’s sterile texts and hastily composed emails seldom replicate the tactility that imbued handwritten letters with gravitas; every flourish, every hesitant stroke, bore the <b>(3) vestiges</b> of a soul laid bare. It is not merely nostalgia that compels some to cling to this endangered practice, but recognition that certain articulations of the heart <b>(4)</b> ___ better when filtered through the slowness of ink and parchment. Indeed, the act of penning a letter demands a kind of <b>(5) deliberateness</b> rare in an age characterized by impulsivity and ephemerality. Though the world races ever forward, perhaps in the margins of our modern lives, the art of letter-writing will preserve a fragile thread tethering us to a slower, richer past.<br><br><br>The word “deliberateness” most nearly means: (5) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Spontaneity"},"2":{"en":"Careful intention"},"3":{"en":"Rapid decision"},"4":{"en":"Emotional outburst"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…the act of penning a letter demands a kind of (5) deliberateness rare in an age characterized by impulsivity and ephemerality.\"</i><br><b>Deliberateness (सोच-समझकर किया गया कार्य)</b> = careful and intentional action. It is set against 'impulsivity'.<br>Spontaneity (स्वाभाविकता, सहजता) – acting without planning; opposite<br>Rapid decision (शीघ्र निर्णय) – opposite of slow care<br>Emotional outburst (भावनात्मक विस्फोट) – unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Careful intention.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000070161","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"What is the correct one-word substitution for \"descent from an ancestor; family or ancestral line\"? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Heritage"},"2":{"en":"Dynasty"},"3":{"en":"Lineage"},"4":{"en":"Legacy"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Lineage (वंश, कुल) = direct descent from an ancestor; ancestral line.</b><br><b>Heritage (विरासत)</b> = traditions, culture or property passed down<br><b>Dynasty (राजवंश)</b> = a line of rulers from the same family<br><b>Legacy (विरासत, धरोहर)</b> = something left behind by a person for later generations<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Lineage.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000070162","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the appropriate adverb.<br><br>The technology has _________ transformed the field of molecular biology. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"marginally"},"2":{"en":"ostensibly"},"3":{"en":"consecutively"},"4":{"en":"irreversibly"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The adverb must suit the strong verb 'transformed' and the sense of permanent change.</b><br><b>Irreversibly (अपरिवर्तनीय रूप से)</b> = in a way that cannot be undone – a technology that transforms a field changes it permanently.<br>Correct sentence: The technology has <b>irreversibly</b> transformed the field of molecular biology.<br><b>Marginally (थोड़ा-सा)</b> – contradicts 'transformed'<br><b>Ostensibly (प्रकट रूप से, दिखावटी तौर पर)</b> – suggests the change is not real<br><b>Consecutively (लगातार क्रम में)</b> – meaningless here<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): irreversibly.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000070163","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Choose the correct direct speech form of the following sentence.<br><br>They asked if I enjoyed working in a fast-paced environment. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They said, \"Do they enjoy working in a fast-paced environment?\""},"2":{"en":"They said, \"Do you like working in fast-paced environments?\""},"3":{"en":"They said, \"Did you like working in a fast-paced environment?\""},"4":{"en":"They said, \"Do you enjoy working in a fast-paced environment?\""}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'asked if' + simple past → a yes/no question in the simple present with 'Do'; 'I' (listener) → 'you'.</b><br>Direct: They said, \"<b>Do you enjoy</b> working in a fast-paced environment?\"<br>Option 1 – 'they' should be 'you'<br>Option 2 – 'enjoy' changed to 'like' and 'environment' to plural<br>Option 3 – 'Did' keeps the past tense and 'enjoy' changed to 'like'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): They said, \"Do you enjoy working in a fast-paced environment?\".</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000070164","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br><br>The expansion of space programs<br>P. has led to discussions on regulatory frameworks,<br>Q. as technological capabilities advance at an unprecedented pace<br>R. among major spacefaring nations and private entities<br>S. ensuring peaceful exploration and equitable resource distribution [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QPSR"},"2":{"en":"PSRQ"},"3":{"en":"SRPQ"},"4":{"en":"RPQS"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: PSRQ</b><br><b>P</b> 'has led to discussions on regulatory frameworks,' gives the verb for the subject.<br><b>S</b> 'ensuring peaceful exploration and equitable resource distribution' tells the purpose of the frameworks.<br><b>R</b> 'among major spacefaring nations and private entities' says between whom.<br><b>Q</b> 'as technological capabilities advance…' gives the time/reason and closes the sentence.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): PSRQ.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000070165","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom \"Best of both worlds\" mean? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Experiencing the advantages of two different situations at the same time"},"2":{"en":"Choosing between two difficult situations"},"3":{"en":"Losing both opportunities due to indecision"},"4":{"en":"Sacrificing one thing to gain another"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Best of both worlds (दोनों तरफ़ से लाभ) = enjoying the benefits of two different things at once.</b><br>Example: Working from a hill-town office gives her the best of both worlds – city pay and village calm.<br>Choosing between two difficult situations (दुविधा) – that is a dilemma<br>Losing both opportunities (दोनों अवसर खोना) – opposite<br>Sacrificing one thing (त्याग करना) – a trade-off, not enjoying both<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Experiencing the advantages of two different situations at the same time.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000070166","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br><br>He was late to an meeting scheduled at 9 AM. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"an"},"2":{"en":"late"},"3":{"en":"meeting"},"4":{"en":"scheduled"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'a' is used before a consonant sound and 'an' before a vowel sound.</b><br>'meeting' begins with the consonant sound /m/, so the article must be 'a'.<br>Correct sentence: He was late to <b>a</b> meeting scheduled at 9 AM.<br>'late', 'meeting' and 'scheduled' are used correctly.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): an.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000070167","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom \"A bolt from the blue\" mean? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A sudden and unexpected event"},"2":{"en":"A predictable outcome"},"3":{"en":"A slow and gradual change"},"4":{"en":"A clear and sunny day"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>A bolt from the blue (अचानक आई विपत्ति/खबर) = something completely sudden and unexpected.</b><br>Example: His resignation came as a bolt from the blue.<br>A predictable outcome (अनुमानित परिणाम) – opposite<br>A slow and gradual change (धीमा परिवर्तन) – opposite of sudden<br>A clear and sunny day (साफ़ धूप वाला दिन) – literal 'blue sky', not the idiom<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): A sudden and unexpected event.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000070168","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Improve the sentence by choosing the correct parts of speech.<br><br>In the beginning of the meeting, there were several misunderstandings due to unclear communication from the head of the department. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"At the beginning of the meeting, there were several misunderstandings due to unclear communication from the head of the department."},"2":{"en":"In the beginning of the meeting, there was several misunderstanding due to unclear communication from the head of the department."},"3":{"en":"At begin of the meeting, there were several misunderstandings due to unclear communication from the head of the department."},"4":{"en":"While beginning of the meeting, there were several misunderstanding due to unclear communication from the head of the department."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'At the beginning of' + a specific event or point; 'In the beginning' (without 'of') means 'at first'.</b><br>The meeting is a specific event, so 'At the beginning of the meeting' is correct.<br>Improved: <b>At the beginning of</b> the meeting, there were several misunderstandings…<br>Option 2 – keeps 'In the beginning of' and 'was several misunderstanding' breaks agreement<br>Option 3 – 'At begin' uses a verb in place of the noun<br>Option 4 – 'While beginning of' is ungrammatical; 'several misunderstanding' needs a plural<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): At the beginning of the meeting, there were several misunderstandings due to unclear communication from the head of the department.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000070169","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?</b><br><br>1. Some theories suggest that language evolved as a tool for social bonding, replacing grooming behavior seen in primates.<br>2. The development of complex language is considered one of the most defining traits of Homo sapiens.<br>3. Archaeological evidence shows that early humans created symbolic representations, such as cave paintings, which indicate the ability to communicate abstract ideas.<br>4. The emergence of language enabled cooperation, cultural transmission, and the rapid expansion of human societies.<br>5. Scientists continue to study the origins of language using genetics, neurology, and comparative studies of primates. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3-2-1-5-4"},"2":{"en":"1-3-4-2-5"},"3":{"en":"2-1-3-4-5"},"4":{"en":"4-3-2-1-5"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-1-3-4-5</b><br><b>2</b> introduces the topic: complex language defines Homo sapiens.<br><b>1</b> gives a theory of how language evolved.<br><b>3</b> adds archaeological evidence of early communication.<br><b>4</b> states the effects of language on human societies.<br><b>5</b> 'Scientists continue to study…' concludes with ongoing research.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 2-1-3-4-5.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000070170","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Which of the following pairs of homonyms can be used to fill in the blanks most suitably?<br><br>The two knights engaged in a fierce _____, using swords with _____ edges. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"dual, duel"},"2":{"en":"duel, duel"},"3":{"en":"dual, dual"},"4":{"en":"duel, dual"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Duel (द्वंद्व युद्ध) = a fight between two people with weapons. Dual (दोहरा) = having two parts.</b><br>Two knights fighting with swords → a fierce <b>duel</b>.<br>Swords with two cutting edges → <b>dual</b> edges.<br>Correct sentence: The two knights engaged in a fierce <b>duel</b>, using swords with <b>dual</b> edges.<br>Options 1, 2 and 3 put 'dual' where a fight is meant or 'duel' where 'two-fold' is meant.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): duel, dual.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000070171","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br><br>He is more smarter than anyone else in class. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"more"},"2":{"en":"anyone"},"3":{"en":"class"},"4":{"en":"smarter"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: A double comparative is wrong – use either '-er' or 'more', never both.</b><br>'smarter' is already comparative, so 'more' must be removed.<br>Correct sentence: He is <b>smarter</b> than anyone else in class.<br>'anyone else' is correct in a comparison within the same group; 'class' is correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): more.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000070172","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correctly spelt word.<br><br>His _________ mannerisms made him a target for ridicule. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"grotesque"},"2":{"en":"grotisque"},"3":{"en":"grottesque"},"4":{"en":"groteseque"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Grotesque (विचित्र, भद्दा) = strange or ugly in a way that is funny or shocking.</b><br>Odd, ugly mannerisms invite ridicule, so the word fits.<br><b>grotisque</b> – 'i' in place of 'e' (grot-e-sque)<br><b>grottesque</b> – double 't'<br><b>groteseque</b> – extra 'e' before 'que'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): grotesque.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000070173","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Intransigent</b> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Unyielding"},"2":{"en":"Flexible"},"3":{"en":"Dogmatic"},"4":{"en":"Obstinate"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Intransigent (हठी, अड़ियल) = refusing to change one's views or agree.</b><br><b>Flexible (लचीला)</b> = willing to change or compromise ✔<br><b>Unyielding (न झुकने वाला)</b> – synonym<br><b>Dogmatic (हठधर्मी)</b> – synonym<br><b>Obstinate (ज़िद्दी)</b> – synonym<br>More antonyms: compliant, accommodating, amenable.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Flexible.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000070174","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Identify the <b>misspelt</b> word. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Licencious"},"2":{"en":"Obsequious"},"3":{"en":"Countenance"},"4":{"en":"Vouchsafe"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Licentious (कामुक, स्वच्छंद) = disregarding moral and sexual rules.</b><br><b>Licencious</b> is misspelt – it ends in '-tious', not '-cious'.<br><b>Obsequious (चापलूस)</b> = too eager to please – correct<br><b>Countenance (चेहरा, मुखाकृति)</b> = face or expression – correct<br><b>Vouchsafe (कृपापूर्वक देना)</b> = to grant something graciously – correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Licencious.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000070175","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the <b>correct spelling</b> of blood-vessel narrowing. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Vasoconstriction"},"2":{"en":"Vasokonstruction"},"3":{"en":"Vasioconstriction"},"4":{"en":"Vasoconstriktian"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Vasoconstriction (रक्त वाहिका संकुचन) = the narrowing of blood vessels.</b><br>It joins vaso (vessel) + constriction (narrowing).<br><b>Vasokonstruction</b> – 'k' for 'c' and 'u' for 'i' (-struction)<br><b>Vasioconstriction</b> – extra 'i' after 'vas'<br><b>Vasoconstriktian</b> – 'k' for 'c' and '-tian' for '-tion'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Vasoconstriction.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000070176","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct <b>one-word substitute</b> for: 'Travelling from place to place for work.' [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Premedieval"},"2":{"en":"Wayfarer"},"3":{"en":"Sedentary"},"4":{"en":"Peripatetic"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Peripatetic (घुमंतू) = travelling from place to place, especially for work.</b><br><b>Premedieval (मध्ययुग-पूर्व)</b> = belonging to the period before the Middle Ages<br><b>Wayfarer (पथिक)</b> = a traveller on foot – a person, not the act of travelling for work<br><b>Sedentary (गतिहीन)</b> = sitting a lot; staying in one place – opposite<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Peripatetic.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000070177","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"<b>Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word:</b><br>The manuscript bore a <b>colophon</b> detailing the scribe’s name. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The typesetter inserted a printer’s colophon on the final page."},"2":{"en":"The insect’s antenna ended in a segmented colophon."},"3":{"en":"The medieval colophon praised the patron."},"4":{"en":"The librarian studied the Syriac colophon."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Colophon (पुस्तक-अंत लेख/मुद्रक-चिह्न) = an inscription or emblem at the end of a book or manuscript giving details of its production.</b><br>Options 1, 3 and 4 use 'colophon' in this same bookish sense – a printer's mark, a medieval inscription, a Syriac manuscript note.<br>Only option 2 uses the word in a different sense, for the end part of an insect's antenna, so it carries the homonym.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The insect’s antenna ended in a segmented colophon.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000070178","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>She <b><i>sings good</i></b> for her age. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"sings greatly"},"2":{"en":"sings nicely"},"3":{"en":"sings well"},"4":{"en":"sings better"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: A verb is modified by an adverb; 'good' is an adjective and 'well' is its adverb.</b><br>'sings' needs the adverb 'well'.<br>Correct sentence: She <b>sings well</b> for her age.<br>sings greatly – 'greatly' means 'to a great degree', not 'skilfully'<br>sings nicely – grammatical but informal; 'well' is the standard adverb of quality<br>sings better – comparative needs 'than'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): sings well.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000070179","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"<b>A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech.</b><br>He said, “What time does the train arrive?” [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He asked what time does the train arrive."},"2":{"en":"He said what time the train had arrived."},"3":{"en":"He asked what time the train arrived."},"4":{"en":"He asked what time the train has arrived."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: said → asked; the Wh-question becomes a statement (subject before verb); simple present → simple past.</b><br>'does the train arrive' → 'the train arrived'.<br>Indirect: He asked what time <b>the train arrived</b>.<br>Option 1 – keeps question word order 'does the train arrive'<br>Option 2 – 'said' not changed to 'asked'; 'had arrived' is the wrong tense<br>Option 4 – 'has arrived' is the wrong tense<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): He asked what time the train arrived.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000070180","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"<b>A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech.</b><br>I said to her, “What are your plans for tomorrow?” [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"I asked her what her plans for the next day were."},"2":{"en":"I told her what were her plans for the next day."},"3":{"en":"I asked her what are her plans for tomorrow."},"4":{"en":"I asked her what her plans were for tomorrow."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: said to → asked; question word order becomes statement order; 'are' → 'were'; 'tomorrow' → 'the next day'.</b><br>'your' → 'her'.<br>Indirect: I asked her what her plans for <b>the next day were</b>.<br>Option 2 – 'told' for a question and 'were her plans' keeps question order<br>Option 3 – 'are' and 'tomorrow' not changed<br>Option 4 – 'tomorrow' not changed to 'the next day'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): I asked her what her plans for the next day were.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};